1
00:00:01,422 --> 00:00:04,222
(Spending This Moment Together)

2
00:00:05,192 --> 00:00:06,862
Nice to see you all.

3
00:00:08,062 --> 00:00:10,491
All right. Last week, Bokdol became a famous dog.

4
00:00:10,492 --> 00:00:12,031
- Right. - My gosh.

5
00:00:12,032 --> 00:00:13,801
Bokdol. Did you sleep well?

6
00:00:13,802 --> 00:00:15,572
(Na Rae's new family member, Bokdol)

7
00:00:16,772 --> 00:00:19,502
(Na Rae used to give him a lot of snacks.)

8
00:00:19,842 --> 00:00:21,002
(Because he slept well.)

9
00:00:21,142 --> 00:00:22,571
(I can't give him snacks when he wakes up? Because he slept well.)

10
00:00:22,572 --> 00:00:24,072
(I clicked the video to see Bokdol, but Na Rae is so cute.)

11
00:00:24,512 --> 00:00:26,081
(- Bokdol has such a cute smile. - Bokdol is smart, cute, and kind.)

12
00:00:26,082 --> 00:00:27,612
(- They're both so lovable. - I hope they're happy together.)

13
00:00:27,852 --> 00:00:29,011
I really appreciated comments like this.

14
00:00:29,012 --> 00:00:30,251
Dog owners with brindle Jindo dogs...

15
00:00:30,252 --> 00:00:31,482
- across Korea wrote... - Yes.

16
00:00:31,622 --> 00:00:34,081
that people were scared when they saw brindle Jindo dogs,

17
00:00:34,082 --> 00:00:36,951
but people are friendly around their dogs and thanked me.

18
00:00:36,952 --> 00:00:38,591
- That's a virtuous cycle. - Bokdol was so gentle.

19
00:00:38,592 --> 00:00:41,491
Bokdol had such kind eyes.

20
00:00:41,492 --> 00:00:42,531
When you were dressing him,

21
00:00:42,532 --> 00:00:44,631
- he was so sweet. - Right.

22
00:00:44,632 --> 00:00:45,801
But you almost lost your hand.

23
00:00:45,802 --> 00:00:47,432
- My gosh. - I can never dress her again.

24
00:00:47,902 --> 00:00:49,701
You're actually missing out on this experience as a dog owner.

25
00:00:49,702 --> 00:00:50,901
There's a certain thrill...

26
00:00:50,902 --> 00:00:51,902
from the fear that you might lose your finger.

27
00:00:51,903 --> 00:00:52,941
Really?

28
00:00:52,942 --> 00:00:54,271
- You can't feel that thrill. - Right.

29
00:00:54,272 --> 00:00:55,371
- My gosh. - It's similar.

30
00:00:55,372 --> 00:00:58,742
Now that she's raising Bokdol, once the weather warms up,

31
00:00:58,912 --> 00:01:00,181
dog owners should get together.

32
00:01:00,182 --> 00:01:01,411
- Yes, let's do something. - Bokdol,

33
00:01:01,412 --> 00:01:02,751
- Comme Des... - Yes.

34
00:01:02,752 --> 00:01:03,851
- That sounds great. - It sounds amazing.

35
00:01:03,852 --> 00:01:06,182
We also have Coco and Kkotbun. Let's get together.

36
00:01:06,352 --> 00:01:07,752
- Call it a Dog Fun Run. - Dog Fun Run.

37
00:01:08,152 --> 00:01:09,391
- Yes. - You put that together right away.

38
00:01:09,392 --> 00:01:11,222
- My gosh. I knew it. Fun Run. - Of course.

39
00:01:11,292 --> 00:01:12,491
Dog Fun Run.

40
00:01:12,492 --> 00:01:14,061
- Gosh, this is so annoying. - I'll be there.

41
00:01:14,062 --> 00:01:15,662
- Dog Fun Run sounds great. - Dog Fun Run.

42
00:01:16,192 --> 00:01:18,402
(The Day Is Coming)

43
00:01:20,932 --> 00:01:23,701
(Sung Hwan wakes up.)

44
00:01:23,702 --> 00:01:24,902
It's Kkotbun.

45
00:01:26,472 --> 00:01:28,212
(Opening up)

46
00:01:28,742 --> 00:01:29,972
Come here, Kkotbun.

47
00:01:31,682 --> 00:01:33,682
(Kkotbun follows Sung Hwan.)

48
00:01:33,842 --> 00:01:34,881
Down.

49
00:01:34,882 --> 00:01:36,151
(Down on her stomach)

50
00:01:36,152 --> 00:01:37,182
Wait.

51
00:01:38,222 --> 00:01:39,421
Don't eat this in one bite.

52
00:01:39,422 --> 00:01:40,582
(Giving her the morning snack)

53
00:01:41,822 --> 00:01:42,822
Wait.

54
00:01:42,952 --> 00:01:44,121
(Bokdol's sister)

55
00:01:44,122 --> 00:01:45,861
- Wait. - Gosh, she's waiting.

56
00:01:45,862 --> 00:01:47,162
Oh, my. How is that possible?

57
00:01:48,832 --> 00:01:50,132
Don't eat that in a hurry.

58
00:01:51,132 --> 00:01:53,501
- She's basically human. - Hey.

59
00:01:53,502 --> 00:01:54,972
As soon as we compliment her...

60
00:01:55,332 --> 00:01:56,332
Darn.

61
00:01:56,333 --> 00:01:57,731
(Excited)

62
00:01:57,732 --> 00:01:59,002
Fine, eat it.

63
00:02:03,312 --> 00:02:06,112
(He grabs the air conditioner filter.)

64
00:02:09,612 --> 00:02:11,722
(He also takes out the blade from the fan.)

65
00:02:12,622 --> 00:02:14,891
(He heads straight to the bathroom.)

66
00:02:14,892 --> 00:02:17,122
Sung Hwan, it looks like you're holding the dumpling steamer.

67
00:02:17,962 --> 00:02:19,121
- You're right. - They look so tasty.

68
00:02:19,122 --> 00:02:20,291
- They look delicious. - There are some dumplings too.

69
00:02:20,292 --> 00:02:21,562
Gosh, they look good.

70
00:02:22,192 --> 00:02:23,332
My gosh.

71
00:02:23,932 --> 00:02:25,832
I'm leaving...

72
00:02:26,032 --> 00:02:30,032
for Kazakhstan to shoot a movie quite soon.

73
00:02:30,372 --> 00:02:31,372
You already shot a movie there...

74
00:02:31,373 --> 00:02:32,742
- a long time ago. - Yes. With Ju Seung.

75
00:02:33,102 --> 00:02:34,102
This is nice.

76
00:02:34,103 --> 00:02:35,911
(Ju Seung and Sung Hwan filmed a movie several years ago.)

77
00:02:35,912 --> 00:02:37,612
That episode was fun. I liked it.

78
00:02:37,842 --> 00:02:39,712
You're a celebrity representing Kazakhstan.

79
00:02:40,442 --> 00:02:42,612
We'll start filming on November 30.

80
00:02:42,812 --> 00:02:44,052
The shoot is for three weeks.

81
00:02:44,482 --> 00:02:45,482
So cute.

82
00:02:45,483 --> 00:02:47,752
- That was Kkotbun. - I thought it was a doll.

83
00:02:48,722 --> 00:02:50,491
I need to use...

84
00:02:50,492 --> 00:02:54,222
the AC and the fan until mid-December.

85
00:02:54,592 --> 00:02:55,962
But I'm leaving soon.

86
00:02:56,332 --> 00:02:58,131
Before I go abroad, I need to clean them.

87
00:02:58,132 --> 00:03:00,662
That way, I'll be happy to see my filter and blade next year.

88
00:03:00,962 --> 00:03:02,871
Given the timeline, I cleaned them today.

89
00:03:02,872 --> 00:03:04,172
You're getting ready for winter.

90
00:03:06,542 --> 00:03:08,712
- Sung Hwan keeps things clean. - He keeps them super clean.

91
00:03:11,442 --> 00:03:13,082
The blade is not even that dusty.

92
00:03:14,952 --> 00:03:16,212
Are you curious about what I'm doing?

93
00:03:16,982 --> 00:03:18,152
Watch what I'm doing.

94
00:03:18,452 --> 00:03:20,182
(Adoring her)

95
00:03:21,552 --> 00:03:23,652
(He uses a toothbrush to clean the filter thoroughly.)

96
00:03:25,022 --> 00:03:27,622
(To have clean filters and blade next year...)

97
00:03:28,362 --> 00:03:29,492
They're all clean now.

98
00:03:30,932 --> 00:03:33,132
(He finishes cleaning them under Kkotbun's watch.)

99
00:03:35,632 --> 00:03:38,872
(How refreshing.)

100
00:03:39,602 --> 00:03:40,672
There.

101
00:03:42,312 --> 00:03:43,541
- Gosh, how neat. - That's neat.

102
00:03:43,542 --> 00:03:45,642
- Right. It won't get dusty then. - You need to cover it up.

103
00:03:48,252 --> 00:03:49,581
(He puts the AC filters in the well-lit balcony.)

104
00:03:49,582 --> 00:03:50,612
My gosh.

105
00:03:53,252 --> 00:03:54,892
I have to do this every year.

106
00:03:56,122 --> 00:03:57,622
This is killing me.

107
00:03:59,792 --> 00:04:00,922
How...

108
00:04:01,992 --> 00:04:04,702
(He sprays the window.)

109
00:04:08,002 --> 00:04:09,901
It's really cold in my house...

110
00:04:09,902 --> 00:04:11,401
- because... - It's drafty in there, right?

111
00:04:11,402 --> 00:04:12,801
- I mean, it gets drafty too. - That...

112
00:04:12,802 --> 00:04:15,541
Because of Kkotbun, I can't keep the boiler on.

113
00:04:15,542 --> 00:04:16,571
- The thing is... - She gets hot, right?

114
00:04:16,572 --> 00:04:17,971
- she gets hot. - I see.

115
00:04:17,972 --> 00:04:19,341
I always keep the heating system...

116
00:04:19,342 --> 00:04:20,711
on the away mode or turn it up by 5°C.

117
00:04:20,712 --> 00:04:21,751
So I can even see my breath.

118
00:04:21,752 --> 00:04:23,511
- Whenever Ju Seung comes over, - Yes.

119
00:04:23,512 --> 00:04:24,782
he tells me he can see his breath.

120
00:04:26,522 --> 00:04:28,521
Insulating the window will be great during winter.

121
00:04:28,522 --> 00:04:30,522
Of course. That's definitely effective.

122
00:04:31,662 --> 00:04:33,661
(Carefully putting it on)

123
00:04:33,662 --> 00:04:35,031
- This... - It's fascinating that...

124
00:04:35,032 --> 00:04:36,091
the sheet doesn't come off.

125
00:04:36,092 --> 00:04:37,232
- My gosh. - It came off.

126
00:04:37,292 --> 00:04:38,601
- It came off. - It came off as soon as he said it.

127
00:04:38,602 --> 00:04:39,602
It's not fascinating at all.

128
00:04:39,603 --> 00:04:41,001
It's like we're jinxing everything today.

129
00:04:41,002 --> 00:04:42,002
(It falls off as soon as he puts it on.)

130
00:04:44,572 --> 00:04:46,772
(Confused)

131
00:04:47,272 --> 00:04:49,242
(Am I doing this right?)

132
00:04:50,042 --> 00:04:51,881
(Coming off)

133
00:04:51,882 --> 00:04:52,912
It didn't stick.

134
00:04:53,712 --> 00:04:56,112
What? Why... What's wrong with this?

135
00:05:00,752 --> 00:05:02,192
- Hello. - Sir.

136
00:05:02,422 --> 00:05:03,422
Yes.

137
00:05:03,692 --> 00:05:04,721
Get 1 of these 2.

138
00:05:04,722 --> 00:05:06,522
Right. The hardware store owner would know everything.

139
00:05:07,162 --> 00:05:09,062
- You know the bubble wrap? - Yes.

140
00:05:09,292 --> 00:05:11,192
I sprayed water and tried to put it up.

141
00:05:11,332 --> 00:05:12,401
You must spray a lot of water.

142
00:05:12,402 --> 00:05:13,861
- A lot of water? - Yes.

143
00:05:13,862 --> 00:05:15,702
Then I failed to adjust the amount of water.

144
00:05:15,832 --> 00:05:17,601
Right. It won't work if you spray only a little bit.

145
00:05:17,602 --> 00:05:19,671
Spray water on the window, but add a bit of detergent in it.

146
00:05:19,672 --> 00:05:21,272
- Detergent? - I see. Detergent.

147
00:05:21,612 --> 00:05:23,612
I'll call you once I finish.

148
00:05:23,912 --> 00:05:25,012
- Okay. - Okay.

149
00:05:25,182 --> 00:05:26,942
(I got it.)

150
00:05:27,912 --> 00:05:29,052
Just one drop?

151
00:05:29,252 --> 00:05:30,252
(Adding detergent just like Sang Sik advised)

152
00:05:30,253 --> 00:05:31,482
Why does he want me to add the detergent?

153
00:05:32,352 --> 00:05:34,752
I think it gets sticky. Detergent might be adhesive.

154
00:05:34,952 --> 00:05:36,352
Okay. That's good.

155
00:05:37,522 --> 00:05:39,892
Just like Sang Sik said, I'll spray a lot of water.

156
00:05:40,522 --> 00:05:43,162
My gosh. Look at this. Great.

157
00:05:44,732 --> 00:05:46,502
(Trying again)

158
00:05:47,702 --> 00:05:49,932
(Carefully pressing on it)

159
00:05:50,102 --> 00:05:52,202
It's working now that I sprayed a lot of water.

160
00:05:52,702 --> 00:05:53,802
I knew we could count on him.

161
00:05:53,902 --> 00:05:56,542
- He's indeed Mr. MacGyver. - Sang Sik knew what to do.

162
00:05:57,712 --> 00:05:58,881
My gosh. I knew I could count...

163
00:05:58,882 --> 00:05:59,981
(I knew I could count on Mr. MacGyver of my neighborhood.)

164
00:05:59,982 --> 00:06:01,282
on Mr. MacGyver of my neighborhood.

165
00:06:02,312 --> 00:06:04,612
(He moves onto the next window.)

166
00:06:05,752 --> 00:06:08,452
My gosh. I won't be able to see my neighbor across the street.

167
00:06:10,092 --> 00:06:11,962
(Ma'am!)

168
00:06:12,292 --> 00:06:13,662
Remember the thing you gave me before?

169
00:06:13,962 --> 00:06:15,632
(The chili peppers weren't spicy at all.)

170
00:06:16,632 --> 00:06:19,962
(The lady across the street was endlessly generous.)

171
00:06:20,462 --> 00:06:22,032
She gave me sweet potatoes and corn.

172
00:06:23,702 --> 00:06:24,772
(Hold on.)

173
00:06:25,102 --> 00:06:26,702
I shouldn't cover up this window.

174
00:06:27,542 --> 00:06:28,711
I won't be able to communicate with her.

175
00:06:28,712 --> 00:06:29,742
You need to communicate with her.

176
00:06:30,642 --> 00:06:31,911
I'll leave this window as it is.

177
00:06:31,912 --> 00:06:34,082
(Carefully leaving the window as it is to communicate)

178
00:06:35,112 --> 00:06:37,682
(He skips over a window and works on the next window.)

179
00:06:39,322 --> 00:06:41,622
(He skillfully puts it on the window now.)

180
00:06:42,792 --> 00:06:46,261
I didn't have any work until my shoot in Kazakhstan.

181
00:06:46,262 --> 00:06:48,361
On my day off, I finished all of my chores.

182
00:06:48,362 --> 00:06:51,132
You have to finish them on your day off.

183
00:06:53,362 --> 00:06:56,372
(He's ready for winter now.)

184
00:06:56,832 --> 00:06:59,101
(That was great.)

185
00:06:59,102 --> 00:07:00,672
It suddenly got cold.

186
00:07:01,472 --> 00:07:02,541
Let's see.

187
00:07:02,542 --> 00:07:04,072
(Taking off)

188
00:07:05,242 --> 00:07:08,752
(He suddenly takes off his sweater.)

189
00:07:09,952 --> 00:07:11,922
(Walking over)

190
00:07:15,752 --> 00:07:18,192
(He's stepping on the scale?)

191
00:07:18,792 --> 00:07:21,931
Three months ago, I got fitted for the outfits in the movie.

192
00:07:21,932 --> 00:07:25,162
I got fitted for the suit and coat. They're already tailored.

193
00:07:25,262 --> 00:07:27,932
But for the past three months,

194
00:07:28,102 --> 00:07:30,432
my weight peaked when it went into the triple digits.

195
00:07:31,202 --> 00:07:32,301
(He was slim three months ago.)

196
00:07:32,302 --> 00:07:34,002
He was so slim back then.

197
00:07:34,302 --> 00:07:36,111
He slowly gained weight.

198
00:07:36,112 --> 00:07:37,741
- My gosh. - Goodness.

199
00:07:37,742 --> 00:07:40,142
Actually, I weigh around 112kg.

200
00:07:40,942 --> 00:07:43,012
My goal is to hit 95kg.

201
00:07:43,082 --> 00:07:45,182
He can't weigh that little given his build.

202
00:07:45,222 --> 00:07:48,252
(Did he reach his goal?)

203
00:07:49,992 --> 00:07:51,122
- My gosh. What? - What?

204
00:07:51,392 --> 00:07:52,461
You didn't put the other foot down, right?

205
00:07:52,462 --> 00:07:54,391
I had been on a diet for 19 days since the 1st.

206
00:07:54,392 --> 00:07:55,561
(His weight goes down to a two-digit number.)

207
00:07:55,562 --> 00:07:57,592
- I lost weight. - You did lose a lot of weight.

208
00:07:58,402 --> 00:08:00,002
(Let me put this on.)

209
00:08:01,362 --> 00:08:03,632
(Satisfied enough)

210
00:08:05,442 --> 00:08:07,072
(What a relief.)

211
00:08:08,972 --> 00:08:11,212
(Opening up)

212
00:08:12,812 --> 00:08:14,281
Two eggs.

213
00:08:14,282 --> 00:08:15,282
(Pondering after grabbing a few eggs)

214
00:08:19,452 --> 00:08:20,952
(Looking in)

215
00:08:24,392 --> 00:08:25,392
(A food tray?)

216
00:08:25,393 --> 00:08:26,462
People use it to lose weight.

217
00:08:27,562 --> 00:08:28,632
You're still trying to lose weight?

218
00:08:29,832 --> 00:08:32,202
(He cuts an apple first.)

219
00:08:32,362 --> 00:08:34,402
This is braised monkfish.

220
00:08:35,802 --> 00:08:37,201
You already mentioned braised monkfish.

221
00:08:37,202 --> 00:08:39,371
Because I get so hungry in the morning when I wake up.

222
00:08:39,372 --> 00:08:40,372
Braised monkfish for breakfast...

223
00:08:40,373 --> 00:08:41,872
- Right. - This is a burger.

224
00:08:43,372 --> 00:08:45,312
- You love burgers too. - I'm crazy about burgers.

225
00:08:45,682 --> 00:08:47,382
This is a burger patty.

226
00:08:47,912 --> 00:08:49,181
There.

227
00:08:49,182 --> 00:08:50,282
(But in reality, he's on a weight-loss diet.)

228
00:08:53,452 --> 00:08:54,952
Gosh, soft-boiled eggs look beautiful.

229
00:08:55,152 --> 00:08:56,321
Presentation matters when we eat.

230
00:08:56,322 --> 00:08:58,822
My gosh. You did a great job boiling the eggs.

231
00:08:59,122 --> 00:09:00,161
- Aren't those store-bought? - Six minutes and thirty seconds.

232
00:09:00,162 --> 00:09:01,191
- Aren't they from a store? - No.

233
00:09:01,192 --> 00:09:02,231
Six minutes and thirty seconds.

234
00:09:02,232 --> 00:09:03,431
- You did a great job. - You boiled them?

235
00:09:03,432 --> 00:09:05,101
- Really? - He did a great job.

236
00:09:05,102 --> 00:09:07,262
- It's hard to nail boiled eggs. - That's amazing.

237
00:09:07,532 --> 00:09:08,672
All right.

238
00:09:08,772 --> 00:09:11,872
(He grabs the food tray and trudges over.)

239
00:09:15,642 --> 00:09:17,542
(A completely healthy meal with black soybean soup)

240
00:09:18,942 --> 00:09:21,652
(Looking simple)

241
00:09:23,682 --> 00:09:24,852
Wait. It's the lady.

242
00:09:28,422 --> 00:09:29,491
The lady...

243
00:09:29,492 --> 00:09:31,292
(Rushing over as he's happy to see her)

244
00:09:31,492 --> 00:09:33,362
- Ma'am! - You startled me.

245
00:09:33,722 --> 00:09:34,792
What are you doing?

246
00:09:34,962 --> 00:09:36,031
I'm making kimchi.

247
00:09:36,032 --> 00:09:37,161
You won't give me any?

248
00:09:37,162 --> 00:09:38,701
Seriously. That lady... You're not looking up...

249
00:09:38,702 --> 00:09:40,202
- on the rooftop, right? - You won't give me any?

250
00:09:40,702 --> 00:09:42,332
- She always shows up around now. - Right.

251
00:09:42,572 --> 00:09:43,772
She's busy. She went back in.

252
00:09:44,472 --> 00:09:45,571
She's like a fairy.

253
00:09:45,572 --> 00:09:48,241
She's like a character in games. What do you call it? NPX?

254
00:09:48,242 --> 00:09:49,312
I wonder what she's doing.

255
00:09:49,472 --> 00:09:52,311
(I should just eat my meal.)

256
00:09:52,312 --> 00:09:53,982
She went back in so fast.

257
00:09:55,112 --> 00:09:56,252
My gosh.

258
00:09:57,312 --> 00:09:59,152
- As soon as you turn on the TV... - That happens to me too.

259
00:09:59,322 --> 00:10:00,481
You'll watch that when you're on a diet?

260
00:10:00,482 --> 00:10:01,751
When I watch during my meals, it feels like...

261
00:10:01,752 --> 00:10:03,052
- I'm eating the same food. - Right.

262
00:10:05,122 --> 00:10:08,362
(Having a bite while pretending to eat the same food)

263
00:10:11,762 --> 00:10:14,232
(You should eat some too.)

264
00:10:16,602 --> 00:10:19,002
(Smacking his lips)

265
00:10:19,872 --> 00:10:21,042
He's eating slowly.

266
00:10:22,672 --> 00:10:23,772
My gosh, ramyeon.

267
00:10:24,512 --> 00:10:25,742
Ramyeon looks so good.

268
00:10:26,442 --> 00:10:28,381
(Looking appetizing)

269
00:10:28,382 --> 00:10:29,711
- What a good way to break the egg. - My gosh.

270
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:30,852
The last time I ate ramyeon was...

271
00:10:32,022 --> 00:10:33,082
three weeks ago.

272
00:10:34,552 --> 00:10:35,652
(Swallowing hard)

273
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:37,191
(Salivating)

274
00:10:37,192 --> 00:10:38,222
Gosh, that looks crazy good.

275
00:10:38,892 --> 00:10:41,832
The lady knows how to present the food beautifully.

276
00:10:43,562 --> 00:10:46,462
(Eating vicariously through the eating show)

277
00:10:48,472 --> 00:10:49,902
(Sighing)

278
00:10:50,472 --> 00:10:52,841
(Oh, poor me.)

279
00:10:52,842 --> 00:10:53,942
Have some too.

280
00:10:54,742 --> 00:10:56,842
- The apple must taste like nothing. - You must overcome this.

281
00:10:58,442 --> 00:10:59,741
(He used to eat everything he wanted.)

282
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:00,812
I remember that day.

283
00:11:01,382 --> 00:11:02,682
- My gosh. - Oh, my.

284
00:11:03,182 --> 00:11:04,352
It's driving me crazy.

285
00:11:04,882 --> 00:11:06,482
(I'm so happy.)

286
00:11:07,552 --> 00:11:09,522
- Your expressions are different. - They're very different.

287
00:11:09,652 --> 00:11:10,722
Right.

288
00:11:11,552 --> 00:11:13,161
- Gosh, that looks good. - Apples are tasty now.

289
00:11:13,162 --> 00:11:14,891
But I wanted ramyeon...

290
00:11:14,892 --> 00:11:16,992
or food with a lot of seasoning in the morning.

291
00:11:17,492 --> 00:11:18,761
(Looking dejected)

292
00:11:18,762 --> 00:11:20,202
Smile when you eat.

293
00:11:21,972 --> 00:11:23,432
- Are you crying? - He'll cry soon.

294
00:11:24,572 --> 00:11:27,342
(He soothes his bitter heart with the soybean soup.)

295
00:11:29,042 --> 00:11:30,842
I'm done too. I finished my meal.

296
00:11:32,882 --> 00:11:34,042
He must feel so empty inside.

297
00:11:34,182 --> 00:11:35,252
I'm done.

298
00:11:35,882 --> 00:11:37,051
Wait.

299
00:11:37,052 --> 00:11:38,982
- Today... - I bet he's ordering food.

300
00:11:39,082 --> 00:11:40,182
He really is.

301
00:11:40,552 --> 00:11:41,652
- I was wrong. - He's...

302
00:11:41,822 --> 00:11:44,152
- I didn't know you kept a log. - Okay. It got into the 90s today.

303
00:11:45,492 --> 00:11:46,861
It's 99.8kg.

304
00:11:46,862 --> 00:11:48,021
(Recording his weight on his phone)

305
00:11:48,022 --> 00:11:49,562
My gosh. On November 1,

306
00:11:51,062 --> 00:11:53,002
my weight was 109.4kg.

307
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:56,032
I lost exactly 10kg within 19 days.

308
00:11:56,972 --> 00:11:59,271
But I don't look so different after this weight loss.

309
00:11:59,272 --> 00:12:00,742
(Feeling upset)

310
00:12:02,842 --> 00:12:04,711
Tomorrow is the 20th.

311
00:12:04,712 --> 00:12:06,341
(His meals for tomorrow are already set.)

312
00:12:06,342 --> 00:12:07,482
A Korean buffet restaurant.

313
00:12:09,112 --> 00:12:12,751
On the 24th, I can have curry rice with scallop.

314
00:12:12,752 --> 00:12:14,122
You're having that on the 24th.

315
00:12:14,722 --> 00:12:16,251
It's an app that helps me lose weight.

316
00:12:16,252 --> 00:12:17,592
It records breakfast, lunch, and dinner.

317
00:12:18,122 --> 00:12:20,192
But I didn't initially use it for my diet.

318
00:12:20,492 --> 00:12:24,592
I usually write down my meals for the week.

319
00:12:24,862 --> 00:12:26,632
The joy of my week...

320
00:12:26,802 --> 00:12:28,301
comes from going to these restaurants.

321
00:12:28,302 --> 00:12:29,872
So I write down what I'm going to eat.

322
00:12:30,072 --> 00:12:33,542
I started writing down my meal plans since 2010...

323
00:12:33,902 --> 00:12:35,042
when I checked the log.

324
00:12:35,102 --> 00:12:36,641
- You kept the log for a long time. - Why do you keep the log?

325
00:12:36,642 --> 00:12:37,642
But why do you look like that?

326
00:12:37,643 --> 00:12:38,881
- This... - "Why do you look like that?"

327
00:12:38,882 --> 00:12:40,541
- "Why do you look like that?" - That app isn't for diet tracking.

328
00:12:40,542 --> 00:12:43,151
I think about what I'm going to eat next week.

329
00:12:43,152 --> 00:12:44,311
- My meals for tomorrow. - He even has meal plans...

330
00:12:44,312 --> 00:12:45,482
for next month.

331
00:12:45,722 --> 00:12:49,492
Sung Hwan showed it to me yesterday at Jang Woo's wedding.

332
00:12:50,022 --> 00:12:51,792
He already planned his meals for the next two months.

333
00:12:52,392 --> 00:12:53,561
- Like what he's going to eat? - Yes.

334
00:12:53,562 --> 00:12:55,091
Ask him to show you his calendar later.

335
00:12:55,092 --> 00:12:56,131
That sounds like a calendar for a drama shoot.

336
00:12:56,132 --> 00:12:57,291
- Two months... - Seriously.

337
00:12:57,292 --> 00:12:59,631
Even housewives won't be able to plan that far ahead.

338
00:12:59,632 --> 00:13:00,902
That's impressive.

339
00:13:01,332 --> 00:13:04,272
Year 2013. Gosh, there it is.

340
00:13:04,872 --> 00:13:06,541
- I got goosebumps too. - My goodness.

341
00:13:06,542 --> 00:13:07,641
You wrote down everything you ate.

342
00:13:07,642 --> 00:13:09,411
"Vegetable bibimbap with instant rice and eggs."

343
00:13:09,412 --> 00:13:11,611
- "Half an apple, cheese..." - "Failed to rebuild my body."

344
00:13:11,612 --> 00:13:13,041
Hold on. At 5:30pm, he had...

345
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:14,341
- "Failed to rebuild my body." - beer, fried chicken,

346
00:13:14,342 --> 00:13:15,651
sausages, and pizza.

347
00:13:15,652 --> 00:13:16,751
- Rebuild... - You're not a cyborg.

348
00:13:16,752 --> 00:13:17,852
Why did you write it like that?

349
00:13:17,982 --> 00:13:19,722
Have you ever succeeded?

350
00:13:20,582 --> 00:13:21,751
(Succeeded to rebuild my body)

351
00:13:21,752 --> 00:13:23,251
- What is this? - "Succeeded to rebuild my body."

352
00:13:23,252 --> 00:13:24,691
- You succeeded? - Yes, I did.

353
00:13:24,692 --> 00:13:26,391
- You had rice balls, spicy pork, - Spicy pork and Pikachu cutlet...

354
00:13:26,392 --> 00:13:27,392
- Pikachu cutlet, - Pikachu cutlet?

355
00:13:27,393 --> 00:13:28,891
chicken and sundae on a stick.

356
00:13:28,892 --> 00:13:30,291
That's about working out.

357
00:13:30,292 --> 00:13:31,931
It's not about losing weight.

358
00:13:31,932 --> 00:13:34,101
- I did CrossFit. It's so intense. - I guess your workout...

359
00:13:34,102 --> 00:13:35,202
- was intense. - It's about that.

360
00:13:35,302 --> 00:13:36,671
(Failed to follow the meal plan and work out)

361
00:13:36,672 --> 00:13:37,832
Gosh, your weight was 93kg.

362
00:13:38,502 --> 00:13:39,541
You lost a lot of weight.

363
00:13:39,542 --> 00:13:41,671
I'm good at losing weight.

364
00:13:41,672 --> 00:13:42,672
(Weight: 93kg)

365
00:13:43,042 --> 00:13:45,412
Kkotbun, we should go out too. Come here.

366
00:13:45,612 --> 00:13:47,942
Let's go. My gosh. Let's go to your favorite spot.

367
00:13:51,682 --> 00:13:52,881
All right.

368
00:13:52,882 --> 00:13:53,882
(Putting on a leash for safety)

369
00:13:53,883 --> 00:13:54,952
Let's go.

370
00:13:55,692 --> 00:13:57,122
- She has her go-to walking route? - Yes.

371
00:13:57,922 --> 00:13:59,122
She only goes there?

372
00:13:59,722 --> 00:14:01,791
- No. We have a lot of routes. - What's this?

373
00:14:01,792 --> 00:14:03,962
- I see. You do. - But we go there most frequently.

374
00:14:05,162 --> 00:14:08,262
(Sung Hwan is going somewhere with Kkotbun.)

375
00:14:08,672 --> 00:14:10,732
(Singing)

376
00:14:10,932 --> 00:14:12,502
(Where are we going?)

377
00:14:13,242 --> 00:14:15,812
(Driving past the bustling city)

378
00:14:16,472 --> 00:14:19,212
(His car heads toward the suburbs.)

379
00:14:21,042 --> 00:14:23,051
(He parks his car in a secluded corner.)

380
00:14:23,052 --> 00:14:24,712
I love you

381
00:14:25,622 --> 00:14:27,551
(Are we here?)

382
00:14:27,552 --> 00:14:28,922
How nice.

383
00:14:29,422 --> 00:14:31,291
All right.

384
00:14:31,292 --> 00:14:33,121
(He gets out of the car with Kkotbun.)

385
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:34,962
My gosh. Let me put on a leash before we go.

386
00:14:37,032 --> 00:14:39,432
(He trudges along with the leash.)

387
00:14:39,832 --> 00:14:42,372
(Barking)

388
00:14:42,672 --> 00:14:43,801
(Saying hello to a dog)

389
00:14:43,802 --> 00:14:45,032
The dog looks like Comme Des.

390
00:14:46,342 --> 00:14:47,342
Let's go.

391
00:14:47,343 --> 00:14:49,212
(Kkotbun, let's walk now.)

392
00:14:49,472 --> 00:14:50,472
(Excited)

393
00:14:50,472 --> 00:14:51,472
Let's go.

394
00:14:51,542 --> 00:14:54,642
Let's go and meet your favorite lady.

395
00:14:55,782 --> 00:14:57,152
Your friends are here.

396
00:14:57,982 --> 00:14:59,082
My gosh, hello.

397
00:14:59,152 --> 00:15:00,152
Oh, my.

398
00:15:00,153 --> 00:15:02,021
Some dogs are happy to interact.

399
00:15:02,022 --> 00:15:03,022
(A dog comes out to say hello to Kkotbun.)

400
00:15:03,022 --> 00:15:04,022
Hello.

401
00:15:04,023 --> 00:15:05,322
(Showing interest)

402
00:15:05,362 --> 00:15:07,291
Pretty soon, Kkotbun and I...

403
00:15:07,292 --> 00:15:10,692
will have to be apart briefly.

404
00:15:10,762 --> 00:15:12,601
I love coming to this park for a reason.

405
00:15:12,602 --> 00:15:15,772
To come here, I have to drive for 20 minutes.

406
00:15:15,972 --> 00:15:18,971
But she can run freely at this park.

407
00:15:18,972 --> 00:15:20,902
- The park is set up nicely. - I'd love to take Bokdol there.

408
00:15:21,342 --> 00:15:22,412
This park is great.

409
00:15:22,672 --> 00:15:24,342
Gosh, Bokdol will have so much fun there.

410
00:15:24,472 --> 00:15:27,542
The space is separated for small and large dogs.

411
00:15:27,812 --> 00:15:30,212
So I bring her here often.

412
00:15:31,282 --> 00:15:33,722
- Hello, sir. - Hello.

413
00:15:34,482 --> 00:15:37,052
Hello. Could you scan her?

414
00:15:37,322 --> 00:15:38,621
- Scan what? - The identification chip...

415
00:15:38,622 --> 00:15:39,921
on her back.

416
00:15:39,922 --> 00:15:40,991
- Did you get one for Bokdol? - Right.

417
00:15:40,992 --> 00:15:42,492
- You need that. - Yes, he got his chip.

418
00:15:43,392 --> 00:15:44,431
Hello.

419
00:15:44,432 --> 00:15:46,601
- Hello. - He's going to the food truck.

420
00:15:46,602 --> 00:15:48,332
- I guess you've been there often. - I go there often.

421
00:15:48,902 --> 00:15:50,632
I'll take this one. Kkotbun likes it.

422
00:15:51,332 --> 00:15:52,641
I'd like a cup of yuzu tea.

423
00:15:52,642 --> 00:15:54,401
Yuzu tea?

424
00:15:54,402 --> 00:15:55,771
(She can't believe her ears.)

425
00:15:55,772 --> 00:15:56,812
Yuzu tea?

426
00:15:57,142 --> 00:15:59,182
I've been on a diet lately.

427
00:15:59,912 --> 00:16:01,981
I'd like yuzu tea and a bit of the fishcake soup.

428
00:16:01,982 --> 00:16:03,582
- Sure. You got it. - Okay.

429
00:16:03,782 --> 00:16:05,621
- What's my total? - It's 7.5 dollars.

430
00:16:05,622 --> 00:16:06,782
It's 7.5 dollars.

431
00:16:06,852 --> 00:16:08,021
I'll give you eight dollars...

432
00:16:08,022 --> 00:16:09,151
- including the fishcake soup. - My gosh.

433
00:16:09,152 --> 00:16:10,622
- It's okay. - Take eight dollars.

434
00:16:11,652 --> 00:16:13,891
By the way, people can eat this too, right?

435
00:16:13,892 --> 00:16:15,092
- Of course. - Yes.

436
00:16:16,932 --> 00:16:18,901
She makes such tasty treats. I'm serious.

437
00:16:18,902 --> 00:16:20,402
- Sweet potatoes? - Yes.

438
00:16:21,762 --> 00:16:23,202
(Humming)

439
00:16:23,402 --> 00:16:25,332
I'm on a diet, but this tastes so good.

440
00:16:27,002 --> 00:16:28,271
- Of course. - Gosh.

441
00:16:28,272 --> 00:16:30,312
That was the tastiest food I had since breakfast that day.

442
00:16:30,672 --> 00:16:32,542
You're stealing her food now that you're on a diet.

443
00:16:33,312 --> 00:16:35,141
You might even end up eating dog food later.

444
00:16:35,142 --> 00:16:37,182
(Joking)

445
00:16:37,612 --> 00:16:40,682
(Warm yuzu tea and fishcake soup are served.)

446
00:16:41,282 --> 00:16:42,822
- Thanks. I'll put them here. - Okay.

447
00:16:44,752 --> 00:16:46,421
(He enters the playground for medium-sized and small dogs.)

448
00:16:46,422 --> 00:16:48,092
My gosh. You look handsome.

449
00:16:49,962 --> 00:16:51,031
(Securing the door)

450
00:16:51,032 --> 00:16:52,832
- This park looks amazing. - This place is great.

451
00:16:52,932 --> 00:16:54,362
I didn't know about this park.

452
00:16:55,262 --> 00:16:56,701
Come here, Kkotbun.

453
00:16:56,702 --> 00:16:57,802
(He puts down Kkotbun in the playground.)

454
00:16:58,842 --> 00:17:00,301
- How nice. - She must be so excited.

455
00:17:00,302 --> 00:17:02,102
- Wait. - She seems interested in Kkotbun.

456
00:17:02,472 --> 00:17:03,942
She wants to say hello.

457
00:17:04,672 --> 00:17:07,682
(The dogs begin sizing up each other out of curiosity.)

458
00:17:08,442 --> 00:17:09,612
(Barking)

459
00:17:10,312 --> 00:17:12,482
What's wrong? Be nice to your friend.

460
00:17:12,952 --> 00:17:14,921
- Kkotbun doesn't want to. - Really?

461
00:17:14,922 --> 00:17:17,192
(Kkotbun, let's have some snacks.)

462
00:17:18,092 --> 00:17:20,422
(Fueling up with the sweet potato snack)

463
00:17:21,892 --> 00:17:23,762
(Kkotbun is running excitedly after the energy boost.)

464
00:17:26,562 --> 00:17:27,832
How adorable.

465
00:17:29,232 --> 00:17:31,232
So many puppies are coming in all of a sudden.

466
00:17:32,572 --> 00:17:34,371
(Kkotbun's buddies flood in.)

467
00:17:34,372 --> 00:17:36,742
Kkotbun, so many of your buddies are here.

468
00:17:36,942 --> 00:17:38,511
Gosh, one of them is wearing sunglasses.

469
00:17:38,512 --> 00:17:40,141
(A cool dog with sunglasses enters.)

470
00:17:40,142 --> 00:17:41,142
- What? - What a cool dog.

471
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:42,852
- That's a cool dog. - They all look so cool.

472
00:17:44,012 --> 00:17:47,221
Come here. My gosh, look at you. You're excited.

473
00:17:47,222 --> 00:17:48,552
(Other dogs flock to him too.)

474
00:17:51,252 --> 00:17:52,691
- Hey. - My gosh.

475
00:17:52,692 --> 00:17:54,021
- Come here. - She won't let them come near you?

476
00:17:54,022 --> 00:17:55,421
- Is she jealous? - That's part of the reason too.

477
00:17:55,422 --> 00:17:56,891
- She's jealous. - She's jealous.

478
00:17:56,892 --> 00:17:57,991
(Exploding with jealousy)

479
00:17:57,992 --> 00:17:59,032
She's jealous.

480
00:17:59,602 --> 00:18:02,272
Gosh, come here. Let's have some snacks.

481
00:18:03,032 --> 00:18:04,672
(Another dog runs toward him.)

482
00:18:04,932 --> 00:18:06,502
Gosh. Let's have some snacks.

483
00:18:06,942 --> 00:18:08,701
(Another puppy is in Sung Hwan's arms.)

484
00:18:08,702 --> 00:18:10,071
- What? - Come here.

485
00:18:10,072 --> 00:18:11,112
(Feeling threatened right away)

486
00:18:12,042 --> 00:18:14,442
(Who are you looking at?)

487
00:18:14,512 --> 00:18:15,512
My gosh.

488
00:18:15,513 --> 00:18:17,782
(Go away!)

489
00:18:18,482 --> 00:18:20,181
Gosh, she's jealous.

490
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:21,282
- Of course. - Come here.

491
00:18:21,722 --> 00:18:22,722
Come here.

492
00:18:22,723 --> 00:18:24,121
(Kkotbun won't leave Sung Hwan's side.)

493
00:18:24,122 --> 00:18:25,152
Come here.

494
00:18:26,022 --> 00:18:27,261
(The unwelcome guest keeps on teasing.)

495
00:18:27,262 --> 00:18:28,822
But she won't bite the other dog.

496
00:18:29,232 --> 00:18:30,931
- She only threatens the dog. - Right, she's all bark and no bite.

497
00:18:30,932 --> 00:18:33,362
When you look at her tail, she's not trying to attack the dog.

498
00:18:33,732 --> 00:18:36,732
(I'm going to protect Sung Hwan!)

499
00:18:37,602 --> 00:18:38,702
Come here.

500
00:18:40,842 --> 00:18:41,901
Are you done playing?

501
00:18:41,902 --> 00:18:43,072
(Quickly dashing over to Sung Hwan's side)

502
00:18:43,172 --> 00:18:45,272
Try to get along with other dogs.

503
00:18:46,382 --> 00:18:49,152
(He holds another puppy in his arms.)

504
00:18:49,512 --> 00:18:51,581
You're quite chubby.

505
00:18:51,582 --> 00:18:53,322
(Staring)

506
00:18:53,422 --> 00:18:54,951
- My gosh. - She's jealous.

507
00:18:54,952 --> 00:18:56,452
Why do you keep holding other dogs?

508
00:18:56,622 --> 00:18:58,021
Do you eat pork belly before going to sleep?

509
00:18:58,022 --> 00:19:00,292
(I'm the only dog he can hold in his arms.)

510
00:19:02,362 --> 00:19:03,531
How beautiful.

511
00:19:03,532 --> 00:19:04,892
(Burning with jealousy)

512
00:19:05,232 --> 00:19:06,361
My goodness.

513
00:19:06,362 --> 00:19:08,402
- Oh, no. Look at her. - She's going away.

514
00:19:08,662 --> 00:19:10,171
- She's sulking. - She's upset.

515
00:19:10,172 --> 00:19:11,301
This isn't right.

516
00:19:11,302 --> 00:19:13,001
- Gosh, she's sulking. - Hey.

517
00:19:13,002 --> 00:19:14,102
(Kkotbun is sulking hard.)

518
00:19:15,202 --> 00:19:17,271
(He's looking for Kkotbun after playing with another dog.)

519
00:19:17,272 --> 00:19:18,442
My gosh, that dog...

520
00:19:19,082 --> 00:19:20,112
Kkotbun.

521
00:19:20,582 --> 00:19:22,412
(Pouting)

522
00:19:22,482 --> 00:19:23,552
Come here.

523
00:19:24,412 --> 00:19:25,412
Come here.

524
00:19:29,452 --> 00:19:30,792
(Heading over)

525
00:19:31,322 --> 00:19:33,522
Come here, Kkotbun. Let me check your belly.

526
00:19:33,722 --> 00:19:35,062
Come here, Kkotbun.

527
00:19:35,992 --> 00:19:38,762
- Gosh, you look so dirty. - She does look dirty.

528
00:19:38,892 --> 00:19:41,362
My gosh. Seriously. Look at you.

529
00:19:41,532 --> 00:19:43,702
Touching your belly after the other dog's belly...

530
00:19:44,772 --> 00:19:46,271
I shouldn't touch a lady's belly?

531
00:19:46,272 --> 00:19:48,002
She doesn't like it when you touch her belly.

532
00:19:49,342 --> 00:19:51,941
You know? You're a beautiful dog.

533
00:19:51,942 --> 00:19:53,482
Look at you.

534
00:19:55,182 --> 00:19:59,152
(Sung Hwan hugs her tightly in his arms.)

535
00:19:59,482 --> 00:20:02,122
(Patting)

536
00:20:02,822 --> 00:20:04,121
- Let's see. - Then...

537
00:20:04,122 --> 00:20:06,561
who's going to look after Kkotbun for three weeks when you're away?

538
00:20:06,562 --> 00:20:09,431
I'm considering to ask my parents to look after her.

539
00:20:09,432 --> 00:20:12,031
Or I could ask her kindergarten since she already goes there.

540
00:20:12,032 --> 00:20:14,161
She wants to play with her friends more.

541
00:20:14,162 --> 00:20:16,101
I'm trying to decide what to do.

542
00:20:16,102 --> 00:20:18,301
I'm considering the dog hotel too...

543
00:20:18,302 --> 00:20:19,971
because they send me photos...

544
00:20:19,972 --> 00:20:21,201
- and videos throughout the stay. - Right.

545
00:20:21,202 --> 00:20:22,471
- That and there are other dogs. - Right.

546
00:20:22,472 --> 00:20:23,741
- Right. - They have a good system.

547
00:20:23,742 --> 00:20:27,282
I'm still worried to be apart from her. I already feel...

548
00:20:28,342 --> 00:20:30,911
I don't have children, but it feels like I'm raising a kid.

549
00:20:30,912 --> 00:20:32,521
- Do you already feel emotional? - Yes.

550
00:20:32,522 --> 00:20:33,622
Yes, I do.

551
00:20:34,522 --> 00:20:36,452
- He does look sad. - Yes.

552
00:20:36,552 --> 00:20:39,161
The last time he went away, it was about a month.

553
00:20:39,162 --> 00:20:40,221
So he cried when he saw her again.

554
00:20:40,222 --> 00:20:42,491
- Right. - He might cry again.

555
00:20:42,492 --> 00:20:44,692
(He cried when he saw Kkotbun after a month.)

556
00:20:46,362 --> 00:20:49,102
(Kkotbun is always so lovable.)

557
00:20:49,302 --> 00:20:52,702
(Half asleep)

558
00:20:52,802 --> 00:20:54,402
Let's go.

559
00:20:54,772 --> 00:20:55,872
Bye.

560
00:20:57,472 --> 00:20:58,912
It tasted great, ma'am.

561
00:20:59,312 --> 00:21:02,582
- Did you have fun? - Yes. My gosh, we had so much fun.

562
00:21:03,252 --> 00:21:04,281
Bye.

563
00:21:04,282 --> 00:21:06,252
- Okay. Bye. - Bye.

564
00:21:07,122 --> 00:21:12,052
(Let's come back next time, Kkotbun.)

565
00:21:13,292 --> 00:21:14,922
(They come back home after a fun day.)

566
00:21:15,222 --> 00:21:16,862
(Groaning)

567
00:21:17,892 --> 00:21:19,262
- She's in his arms. - Gosh.

568
00:21:19,432 --> 00:21:20,602
She's sleepy.

569
00:21:21,162 --> 00:21:22,532
She's already half asleep.

570
00:21:22,972 --> 00:21:24,472
(Grunting)

571
00:21:25,232 --> 00:21:27,241
- Hey. - I also get tired after the trip.

572
00:21:27,242 --> 00:21:28,642
I'm exhausted too, Kkotbun.

573
00:21:28,842 --> 00:21:30,511
Gosh, how will I wash you?

574
00:21:30,512 --> 00:21:31,942
- You have to wash her? - I need to wash you.

575
00:21:32,342 --> 00:21:34,682
(He takes off his jacket first.)

576
00:21:35,412 --> 00:21:37,982
(Sung Hwan sits down.)

577
00:21:39,282 --> 00:21:40,352
Kkotbun.

578
00:21:45,052 --> 00:21:47,822
You know what we're doing with the newspaper on the floor.

579
00:21:49,592 --> 00:21:50,662
You'll groom her?

580
00:21:51,562 --> 00:21:52,732
Gosh, she hates it.

581
00:21:54,062 --> 00:21:56,072
Dogs know everything.

582
00:21:57,402 --> 00:21:58,402
Come here, Kkotbun.

583
00:21:59,242 --> 00:22:00,742
Come. Hurry, Kkotbun.

584
00:22:00,972 --> 00:22:02,042
Hurry.

585
00:22:03,712 --> 00:22:05,411
(I got you.)

586
00:22:05,412 --> 00:22:07,611
- We don't have much time today. - How cute.

587
00:22:07,612 --> 00:22:10,352
What a good girl.

588
00:22:11,252 --> 00:22:12,282
Like this.

589
00:22:12,752 --> 00:22:14,952
- I'm going to... - You'll cut it just like that?

590
00:22:15,182 --> 00:22:16,591
- Really? My gosh. - Gosh.

591
00:22:16,592 --> 00:22:18,352
- You must check the style. Gosh. - Come on.

592
00:22:18,452 --> 00:22:20,592
- I've been doing this for a decade. - Really?

593
00:22:21,522 --> 00:22:22,532
Okay.

594
00:22:23,062 --> 00:22:25,802
My gosh. You look great.

595
00:22:26,402 --> 00:22:28,831
Whether I leave her with my parents or at the dog hotel,

596
00:22:28,832 --> 00:22:30,272
she must look neat.

597
00:22:30,772 --> 00:22:33,572
Kkotbun, you're behaving so well. Oh, my.

598
00:22:33,842 --> 00:22:35,642
You're starting to look more beautiful.

599
00:22:36,272 --> 00:22:38,172
- You've done that a lot. - Gosh, of course.

600
00:22:39,882 --> 00:22:42,112
Kkotbun is such a gentle dog.

601
00:22:42,312 --> 00:22:43,451
Here comes the clipper.

602
00:22:43,452 --> 00:22:45,311
Gosh, I can't even attempt to do that.

603
00:22:45,312 --> 00:22:47,052
- I can't even try using that. - My gosh.

604
00:22:47,652 --> 00:22:49,051
She's usually groomed by a professional,

605
00:22:49,052 --> 00:22:50,421
but I trim around her eyes and nose from time to time.

606
00:22:50,422 --> 00:22:52,392
- For hygiene purposes? - That's all I do. Yes.

607
00:22:53,762 --> 00:22:57,332
I need to take good care of you while I'm in Korea.

608
00:22:57,832 --> 00:22:59,202
Here it comes again.

609
00:22:59,962 --> 00:23:01,761
- I knew it. - It's starting.

610
00:23:01,762 --> 00:23:03,731
- My gosh. - She doesn't like that.

611
00:23:03,732 --> 00:23:05,572
So how were the other puppies today?

612
00:23:06,442 --> 00:23:08,041
(You adored only other dogs. I'm upset.)

613
00:23:08,042 --> 00:23:09,571
- But she's still gentle. - That's it.

614
00:23:09,572 --> 00:23:11,042
She only growled. How nice of her.

615
00:23:11,572 --> 00:23:14,181
I see, Kkotbun. That's how you felt.

616
00:23:14,182 --> 00:23:15,881
That's my skill.

617
00:23:15,882 --> 00:23:17,952
- You have to baby her. - You're almost done.

618
00:23:19,822 --> 00:23:20,951
She's so cute.

619
00:23:20,952 --> 00:23:22,652
(His grooming skills are smooth.)

620
00:23:23,152 --> 00:23:24,892
Well done.

621
00:23:25,622 --> 00:23:27,222
My gosh. Who's this?

622
00:23:28,292 --> 00:23:30,292
(Her beauty just leveled up.)

623
00:23:31,132 --> 00:23:33,402
Isn't it nice to get your hair trimmed?

624
00:23:34,502 --> 00:23:36,201
Kkotbun, listen. Here's the thing.

625
00:23:36,202 --> 00:23:38,671
- Dogs are our forever friends. - Yes, that's right.

626
00:23:38,672 --> 00:23:40,571
Let's go and take a half-body bath which you love.

627
00:23:40,572 --> 00:23:42,072
She loves doing half-body baths?

628
00:23:42,302 --> 00:23:44,272
She doesn't like full-body baths, but she likes half-body baths.

629
00:23:44,972 --> 00:23:46,381
- Gosh, really? - Yes.

630
00:23:46,382 --> 00:23:47,912
- Her body must ache too. - Yes.

631
00:23:48,142 --> 00:23:49,851
We can wash ourselves.

632
00:23:49,852 --> 00:23:51,781
Dogs don't seem to like it because we have to do it for them.

633
00:23:51,782 --> 00:23:54,552
- Would you like it if I washed you? - Right. They don't like it.

634
00:23:54,952 --> 00:23:56,521
- What are you talking about? - What are you saying?

635
00:23:56,522 --> 00:23:57,522
He's not a dog.

636
00:23:57,523 --> 00:23:59,321
If it's done by a professional, she might like it.

637
00:23:59,322 --> 00:24:00,861
Why is he comparing Ju Seung to a dog?

638
00:24:00,862 --> 00:24:02,291
- I'm sorry. - He's a human.

639
00:24:02,292 --> 00:24:03,492
(I'm sorry, Ju Seung.)

640
00:24:04,962 --> 00:24:06,632
(Gushing out)

641
00:24:06,662 --> 00:24:08,832
Come here, Kkotbun. Hurry.

642
00:24:09,502 --> 00:24:10,972
Come here. Hurry up.

643
00:24:11,872 --> 00:24:13,202
(Lifting her)

644
00:24:13,972 --> 00:24:15,442
Gosh. It's nice and warm.

645
00:24:16,872 --> 00:24:18,441
- Once their coat gets wet, - How nice.

646
00:24:18,442 --> 00:24:20,182
- their true body shape shows. - Gosh, how nice.

647
00:24:20,512 --> 00:24:22,511
How nice. Isn't it nice?

648
00:24:22,512 --> 00:24:24,881
It can't be too hot or too cold.

649
00:24:24,882 --> 00:24:27,451
The perfect temperature is about 38°C.

650
00:24:27,452 --> 00:24:29,922
Then I add the bath powder for bubbles...

651
00:24:30,022 --> 00:24:31,051
which I don't even use for myself.

652
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:32,391
- You have to add that. - That's nice.

653
00:24:32,392 --> 00:24:34,262
- You must add that. - I put in vegan shampoo too.

654
00:24:34,362 --> 00:24:36,192
I add everything and give her a half-body bath.

655
00:24:38,362 --> 00:24:39,362
(Snoring)

656
00:24:41,532 --> 00:24:42,902
I'll play your favorite music.

657
00:24:44,272 --> 00:24:45,701
Apparently, classical music is good for the dogs.

658
00:24:45,702 --> 00:24:47,702
- Dogs like it. - I learned that.

659
00:24:47,872 --> 00:24:48,942
How nice.

660
00:24:50,312 --> 00:24:51,512
Go to sleep.

661
00:24:52,242 --> 00:24:53,312
Go to sleep.

662
00:24:54,082 --> 00:24:55,811
Oh, my.

663
00:24:55,812 --> 00:24:57,411
(Blinking)

664
00:24:57,412 --> 00:24:59,651
- You see the shape of her body. - She's sleepy.

665
00:24:59,652 --> 00:25:01,152
Dogs really do that.

666
00:25:02,952 --> 00:25:04,791
(Gosh, Kkotbun.)

667
00:25:04,792 --> 00:25:06,161
She's sleepy.

668
00:25:06,162 --> 00:25:08,022
(You're sleepy.)

669
00:25:08,762 --> 00:25:10,262
She looks like she has gone through a breakup.

670
00:25:11,232 --> 00:25:12,932
(My Kkotbun)

671
00:25:13,702 --> 00:25:16,172
- I think she's sleeping. - She's very tired.

672
00:25:16,472 --> 00:25:18,671
Sung Hwan, if Kkotbun likes the half bath,

673
00:25:18,672 --> 00:25:21,301
you should put a plushie that comes up to here.

674
00:25:21,302 --> 00:25:22,641
Then she'll lean on it and nap for a while.

675
00:25:22,642 --> 00:25:25,412
My goodness. That's a great tip.

676
00:25:25,612 --> 00:25:27,842
Shall we wash up, Kkotbun? Let's wash up.

677
00:25:30,482 --> 00:25:32,821
(He massages Kkotbun in an experienced way.)

678
00:25:32,822 --> 00:25:34,021
She's so tiny.

679
00:25:34,022 --> 00:25:35,622
- How cute. She's so tiny. - That's right.

680
00:25:36,752 --> 00:25:37,821
Hey, now...

681
00:25:37,822 --> 00:25:38,822
(Shaking off water)

682
00:25:38,823 --> 00:25:41,092
- Hey, now... - It's refreshing.

683
00:25:42,862 --> 00:25:44,462
(It's understandable.)

684
00:25:45,792 --> 00:25:47,701
- It can't be helped. - Dog mist.

685
00:25:47,702 --> 00:25:50,032
You need to be prepared to get wet.

686
00:25:50,932 --> 00:25:52,702
It'll take forever to dry you off.

687
00:25:55,642 --> 00:25:56,812
All right.

688
00:25:58,442 --> 00:26:00,381
Kkotbun, I'm exhausted too.

689
00:26:00,382 --> 00:26:02,482
(I'm exhausted.)

690
00:26:03,382 --> 00:26:04,481
Oh, my,

691
00:26:04,482 --> 00:26:05,682
(Groaning)

692
00:26:06,152 --> 00:26:07,222
Oh, my,

693
00:26:07,952 --> 00:26:09,052
Oh, my,

694
00:26:09,792 --> 00:26:10,821
Okay.

695
00:26:10,822 --> 00:26:12,191
(You shouldn't catch a cold.)

696
00:26:12,192 --> 00:26:13,862
Gosh, Kkotbun.

697
00:26:13,962 --> 00:26:16,492
Let's get dried up. Come here.

698
00:26:17,332 --> 00:26:21,162
The wind is strong, so you'll get dried up in no time.

699
00:26:23,272 --> 00:26:24,932
(Drying)

700
00:26:26,372 --> 00:26:28,472
Kkotbun is staying still.

701
00:26:29,272 --> 00:26:31,872
You're getting dried up in no time since the wind is strong.

702
00:26:32,442 --> 00:26:33,582
You're becoming fluffy.

703
00:26:34,412 --> 00:26:36,912
It's very convenient since the hair dryer can stand.

704
00:26:37,482 --> 00:26:39,552
You got dried up in no time thanks to this product.

705
00:26:40,022 --> 00:26:42,121
(Fluffy)

706
00:26:42,122 --> 00:26:43,522
(He sprays some mist.)

707
00:26:44,452 --> 00:26:45,922
All done.

708
00:26:46,522 --> 00:26:48,562
- Kkotbun is gentle. - I'm jealous.

709
00:26:48,922 --> 00:26:50,692
I'll wash up and head out.

710
00:26:52,462 --> 00:26:55,031
- Kkotbun, I'll play some music. - That's right.

711
00:26:55,032 --> 00:26:56,202
- Let's go. - She's clean.

712
00:26:56,802 --> 00:26:58,332
- She's fluffy. - She's looking at her dad only.

713
00:26:58,702 --> 00:26:59,972
I'll be back.

714
00:27:00,802 --> 00:27:02,041
I'm running late.

715
00:27:02,042 --> 00:27:03,542
(Sung Hwan plays the music and heads out hurriedly.)

716
00:27:04,672 --> 00:27:06,342
Let's go. I'll be back, Kkotbun.

717
00:27:09,142 --> 00:27:10,752
(Pressing)

718
00:27:11,812 --> 00:27:14,652
They'll scold me for being late.

719
00:27:15,682 --> 00:27:17,291
- I need to hurry up. - Where is he going?

720
00:27:17,292 --> 00:27:19,222
- Are those presents? - Let's go.

721
00:27:21,262 --> 00:27:22,522
Gosh, it smells nice.

722
00:27:22,722 --> 00:27:24,361
- The budae jjigae place looks good. - I love budae jjigae.

723
00:27:24,362 --> 00:27:25,562
Budae jjigae is tasty.

724
00:27:25,832 --> 00:27:29,332
(Singing)

725
00:27:30,302 --> 00:27:31,702
I'm here.

726
00:27:33,772 --> 00:27:36,341
(Sung Hwan enters a place.)

727
00:27:36,342 --> 00:27:37,572
Where is he going?

728
00:27:38,472 --> 00:27:40,912
- Hello. - Hello.

729
00:27:41,282 --> 00:27:42,642
- Oysters. - Yellowtail.

730
00:27:42,812 --> 00:27:44,451
- Crabs. - My goodness.

731
00:27:44,452 --> 00:27:45,512
Yellowtail.

732
00:27:46,382 --> 00:27:47,682
They're in season.

733
00:27:48,682 --> 00:27:49,722
Mom.

734
00:27:53,262 --> 00:27:54,962
- "Mom?" - It must be his mom.

735
00:27:56,862 --> 00:27:58,892
Hey, you didn't give me a single call.

736
00:27:59,132 --> 00:28:01,532
- Yes, I did. - You just left instant messages.

737
00:28:01,662 --> 00:28:03,631
- I called you last time. - What?

738
00:28:03,632 --> 00:28:04,831
She's Ju Seung's mom.

739
00:28:04,832 --> 00:28:06,272
What is my mom doing there?

740
00:28:07,942 --> 00:28:10,072
Hey, you didn't give me a single call.

741
00:28:10,272 --> 00:28:12,612
- Yes, I did. - You just left instant messages.

742
00:28:12,772 --> 00:28:14,881
- I called you last time. - What?

743
00:28:14,882 --> 00:28:16,011
She's Ju Seung's mom.

744
00:28:16,012 --> 00:28:17,852
I brought you a present for you.

745
00:28:18,552 --> 00:28:19,782
She's Ju Seung's mom.

746
00:28:20,182 --> 00:28:22,722
I went there to see Ms. Jeon-ja Gwi Sim.

747
00:28:23,252 --> 00:28:24,392
(What's your mother's name?)

748
00:28:25,022 --> 00:28:27,462
(It's Jeon-ja Gwi Sim-ja.)

749
00:28:28,392 --> 00:28:30,492
(Shouldn't you say, "Jeon Gwi-ja Sim-ja?")

750
00:28:31,532 --> 00:28:34,131
(He made it sound like "Electronic ghost.")

751
00:28:34,132 --> 00:28:36,172
- Jeon-ja Gwi Sim. - Ms. Jeon-ja Gwi Sim.

752
00:28:36,732 --> 00:28:39,471
You know, I want to say something.

753
00:28:39,472 --> 00:28:42,102
- Just don't. - It has been many years...

754
00:28:42,542 --> 00:28:43,542
since I've said her name.

755
00:28:43,543 --> 00:28:45,011
I wondered what "Jeon-ja Gwi Sim" meant.

756
00:28:45,012 --> 00:28:47,181
- What's "Jeon-ja Gwi Sim?" - It sounded like a modern ghost.

757
00:28:47,182 --> 00:28:49,681
I thought her last name had two syllables like Namkoong.

758
00:28:49,682 --> 00:28:51,312
- Jeon-ja. - Same here.

759
00:28:51,452 --> 00:28:53,722
The kind of last names only 1 or 2 people have in Korea.

760
00:28:53,882 --> 00:28:55,481
I knew her name,

761
00:28:55,482 --> 00:28:57,792
so I was like, "What? Did she change her name?"

762
00:28:58,292 --> 00:28:59,692
To Jeon-ja Gwi Sim?

763
00:29:00,022 --> 00:29:02,061
That's why people call her Madame Digital these days.

764
00:29:02,062 --> 00:29:03,191
Madame Digital.

765
00:29:03,192 --> 00:29:05,162
- That's right. - Madame Digital sounds hip.

766
00:29:06,632 --> 00:29:08,501
(Madame Digital is close to Sung Hwan, Ju Seung's best friend.)

767
00:29:08,502 --> 00:29:10,902
(Sung Hwan, Gwi Sim, Ju Seung)

768
00:29:11,032 --> 00:29:12,572
Sung Hwan was so skinny.

769
00:29:13,602 --> 00:29:15,702
- Mom was young back then. - I know.

770
00:29:16,542 --> 00:29:18,342
Of course, we became close through Ju Seung.

771
00:29:18,472 --> 00:29:21,581
Mom is completely open-minded.

772
00:29:21,582 --> 00:29:23,252
She's practically a friend of mine.

773
00:29:23,482 --> 00:29:25,451
There's nothing we don't talk about.

774
00:29:25,452 --> 00:29:27,751
We're friends who talk about anything and everything.

775
00:29:27,752 --> 00:29:29,082
That's incredible.

776
00:29:29,322 --> 00:29:31,822
I'm close to Ju Seung's mom...

777
00:29:32,292 --> 00:29:34,891
because her place was a hideout when Ju Seung lived with her.

