00:48:48,442 --> 00:48:49,511
(His mouth is already watering.)

1290
00:48:49,512 --> 00:48:50,682
It looks amazing.

1291
00:48:54,552 --> 00:48:55,751
(The gold cheese becomes one with the bulgogi.)

1292
00:48:55,752 --> 00:48:57,182
- Gosh! - That looks delicious.

1293
00:48:57,952 --> 00:48:59,351
That looks delicious.

1294
00:48:59,352 --> 00:49:01,192
That's like a bulgogi burger.

1295
00:49:03,822 --> 00:49:05,392
He might gain a lot of weight.

1296
00:49:06,632 --> 00:49:09,832
- Gosh! - I used low-sugar bulgogi.

1297
00:49:09,862 --> 00:49:11,832
I used allulose instead of sugar.

1298
00:49:12,572 --> 00:49:14,342
- We all love allulose. - Right.

1299
00:49:14,442 --> 00:49:16,202
Even the bread is low on sugar.

1300
00:49:16,702 --> 00:49:19,742
It has less than a bowl of rice of calories.

1301
00:49:19,972 --> 00:49:21,011
(Fascinated)

1302
00:49:21,012 --> 00:49:23,742
Why are you so obsessed with low-sugar food?

1303
00:49:23,782 --> 00:49:26,682
It's the least I can do to keep my conscience.

1304
00:49:27,082 --> 00:49:28,852
I understand.

1305
00:49:29,452 --> 00:49:31,451
But won't it become massive when everything is gathered?

1306
00:49:31,452 --> 00:49:33,922
When low-sugar foods come together, they become high-sugar food.

1307
00:49:34,522 --> 00:49:36,122
(That's a great way to put it!)

1308
00:49:37,662 --> 00:49:40,832
(He made the cheese bulgogi sandwich in a flash.)

1309
00:49:42,932 --> 00:49:44,302
(Opening)

1310
00:49:47,702 --> 00:49:49,172
They're all low-sugar sauces.

1311
00:49:49,972 --> 00:49:51,812
Ten low-sugar items add up to become high in sugar.

1312
00:49:52,972 --> 00:49:55,682
(He has various types of sauces.)

1313
00:49:56,412 --> 00:49:58,552
(Along with low-sugar and low-calorie sauces,)

1314
00:49:59,552 --> 00:50:02,522
(his half-cheat day breakfast is ready.)

1315
00:50:03,752 --> 00:50:05,492
I'll start eating now.

1316
00:50:07,492 --> 00:50:08,992
He's eating really early.

1317
00:50:09,962 --> 00:50:11,362
(Pressing the remote control)

1318
00:50:14,162 --> 00:50:15,461
Starting from now...

1319
00:50:15,462 --> 00:50:16,462
(He starts eating after turning on the TV.)

1320
00:50:18,302 --> 00:50:19,332
What is that?

1321
00:50:19,502 --> 00:50:21,542
That is the garlic dipping sauce.

1322
00:50:21,842 --> 00:50:22,902
Gosh.

1323
00:50:23,272 --> 00:50:24,771
I wanted it to be tasty,

1324
00:50:24,772 --> 00:50:27,142
but I had to think about my health as well.

1325
00:50:29,342 --> 00:50:31,582
Gosh, you're eating so well.

1326
00:50:32,352 --> 00:50:33,352
Gosh!

1327
00:50:34,012 --> 00:50:35,022
Gosh!

1328
00:50:36,752 --> 00:50:37,952
It's insane.

1329
00:50:40,422 --> 00:50:41,462
Monde.

1330
00:50:42,462 --> 00:50:44,062
I'm so happy right now.

1331
00:50:47,802 --> 00:50:49,161
This time, it's the low-sugar chipotle sauce.

1332
00:50:49,162 --> 00:50:50,632
There's a low-sugar chipotle sauce?

1333
00:50:50,762 --> 00:50:52,071
There's even a low-sugar Bburinkle sauce.

1334
00:50:52,072 --> 00:50:53,072
Right.

1335
00:50:53,602 --> 00:50:54,972
That's crazy.

1336
00:50:56,342 --> 00:50:57,811
(His feet bounce up and down in joy.)

1337
00:50:57,812 --> 00:50:59,072
So that was what I did.

1338
00:51:00,242 --> 00:51:01,612
(Focused)

1339
00:51:05,682 --> 00:51:06,711
That looks really good.

1340
00:51:06,712 --> 00:51:08,451
- I love doing that as well! - Right?

1341
00:51:08,452 --> 00:51:10,581
- Gosh! - Watching food videos.

1342
00:51:10,582 --> 00:51:12,952
You're watching pastry videos that early in the morning?

1343
00:51:14,152 --> 00:51:15,962
(It's currently 6:50am.)

1344
00:51:16,092 --> 00:51:17,631
- Right. - Gosh.

1345
00:51:17,632 --> 00:51:20,162
- You must really like bread. - I love bread.

1346
00:51:21,862 --> 00:51:23,862
(Bread instead of rice for breakfast)

1347
00:51:25,432 --> 00:51:27,202
(Putting in his mouth)

1348
00:51:29,942 --> 00:51:31,971
That must feel so dry. You must have some soup.

1349
00:51:31,972 --> 00:51:34,072
- We're the ones who prefer rice. - Right.

1350
00:51:34,582 --> 00:51:36,681
There should be an onion soup, at least.

1351
00:51:36,682 --> 00:51:38,452
- Gosh, an onion soup. - Right.

1352
00:51:38,652 --> 00:51:39,851
There must be low-sugar onion soups as well.

1353
00:51:39,852 --> 00:51:41,221
- Right. - Low-sugar onion soups?

1354
00:51:41,222 --> 00:51:42,282
I'm sure you can find them.

1355
00:51:42,622 --> 00:51:44,391
I've seen up to low-sugar kkanpunggis.

1356
00:51:44,392 --> 00:51:45,992
- Gosh. - That's the winner.

1357
00:51:46,052 --> 00:51:48,421
It's that one, isn't it? The one with Seongsu-dong in its name.

1358
00:51:48,422 --> 00:51:50,821
Yes! You're right!

1359
00:51:50,822 --> 00:51:52,232
I eat that often.

1360
00:51:52,462 --> 00:51:54,531
- It's good. - It's actually a thing?

1361
00:51:54,532 --> 00:51:56,461
- Yes. - It wasn't a joke?

1362
00:51:56,462 --> 00:51:58,101
There's everything you can imagine.

1363
00:51:58,102 --> 00:52:00,471
Low-sugar kkanpunggi, low-sugar yukgaejang,

1364
00:52:00,472 --> 00:52:02,101
low-sugar tangsuyuk, and low-sugar jokbal.

1365
00:52:02,102 --> 00:52:03,601
- What? - Right.

1366
00:52:03,602 --> 00:52:05,071
There's even low-sugar chicken feet.

1367
00:52:05,072 --> 00:52:06,371
- Gosh. - No way.

1368
00:52:06,372 --> 00:52:08,242
Are there no low-sugar phones?

1369
00:52:08,382 --> 00:52:10,682
- I'm pretty sure you can find them. - No low-sugar laptops?

1370
00:52:10,742 --> 00:52:13,282
The screen brightness is quite low for those phones.

1371
00:52:14,152 --> 00:52:15,451
There are even low-sugar nuggets.

1372
00:52:15,452 --> 00:52:17,321
- Gosh! - They taste just the same.

1373
00:52:17,322 --> 00:52:19,122
Gosh, why does that word annoy me so much? "Low-sugar."

1374
00:52:19,152 --> 00:52:21,492
It feels just as annoying as the Fun Run.

1375
00:52:23,162 --> 00:52:25,031
- So that was what it felt like. - He overcame himself.

1376
00:52:25,032 --> 00:52:26,462
You learned what it felt like today.

1377
00:52:27,662 --> 00:52:29,262
(The low-sugar food lover finished his meal well.)

1378
00:52:30,402 --> 00:52:31,672
(Rushing over)

1379
00:52:33,932 --> 00:52:35,872
(He washes the dishes right away after eating.)

1380
00:52:37,642 --> 00:52:39,372
(Wiping)

1381
00:52:39,712 --> 00:52:41,582
(He cleans up right away as well.)

1382
00:52:43,212 --> 00:52:45,082
- Gosh. - He's really neat.

1383
00:52:45,682 --> 00:52:47,512
(He opens the freezer this time.)

1384
00:52:49,882 --> 00:52:52,191
(He gets something out from the freezer.)

1385
00:52:52,192 --> 00:52:54,392
- Is he eating again? - It's bread.

1386
00:52:54,962 --> 00:52:56,491
This guy is amazing.

1387
00:52:56,492 --> 00:52:57,962
He must really love bread.

1388
00:52:59,492 --> 00:53:01,962
(It heads into the air fryer to get heated up.)

1389
00:53:02,402 --> 00:53:04,902
(Thinking)

1390
00:53:05,732 --> 00:53:08,002
(He gets something else out from the freezer.)

1391
00:53:08,102 --> 00:53:10,372
- What is that? Ice cream? - Tofu?

1392
00:53:11,272 --> 00:53:13,212
(Is that for me?)

1393
00:53:14,542 --> 00:53:15,642
Ice cream.

1394
00:53:15,912 --> 00:53:17,381
- Is it bread again? - Bread again?

1395
00:53:17,382 --> 00:53:18,512
(More bread appears.)

1396
00:53:19,652 --> 00:53:21,582
(He eats another type of bread while heating up the bread.)

1397
00:53:23,482 --> 00:53:25,052
That one looks good.

1398
00:53:25,192 --> 00:53:26,492
It's really good.

1399
00:53:26,722 --> 00:53:27,991
Do you know White Windmill?

1400
00:53:27,992 --> 00:53:29,492
- Of course, I do! - You do?

1401
00:53:29,592 --> 00:53:31,761
People wait in long lines for that.

1402
00:53:31,762 --> 00:53:33,361
- Right. - What is that?

1403
00:53:33,362 --> 00:53:34,561
Is that a low-sugar windmill?

1404
00:53:34,562 --> 00:53:35,631
No.

1405
00:53:35,632 --> 00:53:36,632
It's not?

1406
00:53:36,633 --> 00:53:38,371
It sounds like it will turn really slowly.

1407
00:53:38,372 --> 00:53:39,972
- That must be frustrating. - That must be frustrating.

1408
00:53:42,072 --> 00:53:43,072
(Give me some as well.)

1409
00:53:43,073 --> 00:53:44,272
I'm sorry, Monde.

1410
00:53:45,142 --> 00:53:46,272
You little rascal.

1411
00:53:47,712 --> 00:53:50,212
After I finish this, I'll bring out your favorite.

1412
00:53:53,012 --> 00:53:54,182
How adorable.

1413
00:53:55,982 --> 00:53:57,622
(It's ready.)

1414
00:53:58,852 --> 00:54:00,492
(He has his 3rd type of bread at 7:05am.)

1415
00:54:04,322 --> 00:54:05,491
- Gosh. - It's a croissant.

1416
00:54:05,492 --> 00:54:06,892
- It looks like... - What is that?

1417
00:54:07,802 --> 00:54:10,231
That's the 10,000-layer croissant.

1418
00:54:10,232 --> 00:54:12,272
You can add cream to it as well.

1419
00:54:12,732 --> 00:54:15,172
Is it fresh cream or cream cheese?

1420
00:54:15,402 --> 00:54:18,342
I added fresh cream, custard cream, and vanilla beans.

1421
00:54:18,872 --> 00:54:20,512
- Okay. So that's what it's like. - Right.

1422
00:54:23,112 --> 00:54:24,112
(Crunchy)

1423
00:54:27,752 --> 00:54:30,022
(It's so good.)

1424
00:54:32,822 --> 00:54:34,962
Actually, I'm a big bread lover.

1425
00:54:35,792 --> 00:54:37,932
Ever since I was young, my mother...

1426
00:54:38,392 --> 00:54:40,531
brought home this much bread.

1427
00:54:40,532 --> 00:54:44,232
She bought all kinds of bread and cut them all up.

1428
00:54:44,572 --> 00:54:45,932
I finished all of them in a single day.

1429
00:54:46,672 --> 00:54:48,242
I think that was when...

1430
00:54:49,072 --> 00:54:50,342
I started liking bread.

1431
00:54:51,212 --> 00:54:52,212
(Licking his lips)

1432
00:54:53,942 --> 00:54:56,312
- It's filled with bread. - It's my bread freezer.

1433
00:54:56,712 --> 00:54:57,782
It's all bread.

1434
00:54:59,952 --> 00:55:01,052
This is insane.

1435
00:55:02,522 --> 00:55:03,622
It's so good.

1436
00:55:04,552 --> 00:55:05,752
I should order some more.

1437
00:55:06,492 --> 00:55:07,991
(Choose your order.)

1438
00:55:07,992 --> 00:55:09,062
What is that?

1439
00:55:09,662 --> 00:55:11,132
- I ordered more. - You're ordering more?

1440
00:55:11,332 --> 00:55:14,292
Were you possessed by a ghost that died while craving bread?

1441
00:55:14,392 --> 00:55:16,231
People who love bread...

1442
00:55:16,232 --> 00:55:17,501
go on a bread pilgrimage.

1443
00:55:17,502 --> 00:55:19,771
They go on trips to places where there are bakeries.

1444
00:55:19,772 --> 00:55:20,831
- Right. - Bread pilgrimage?

1445
00:55:20,832 --> 00:55:22,502
- Bread pilgrimage? - I go on bread pilgrimages.

1446
00:55:22,642 --> 00:55:25,072
There's the Bread Taxi...

1447
00:55:25,212 --> 00:55:27,041
- and Bread Bus in Daejeon. - Bread Bus?

1448
00:55:27,042 --> 00:55:28,111
Because of Sungsimdang?

1449
00:55:28,112 --> 00:55:30,981
They go to the top bakeries in Daejeon.

1450
00:55:30,982 --> 00:55:33,081
- Gosh. - There's a unique world for that.

1451
00:55:33,082 --> 00:55:34,112
Right.

1452
00:55:35,352 --> 00:55:38,221
(The third type of bread disappears in a flash.)

1453
00:55:38,222 --> 00:55:39,222
(The fourth type of bread appears.)

1454
00:55:39,223 --> 00:55:40,392
More?

1455
00:55:40,522 --> 00:55:42,291
You must know this. It's the condensed milk baguette...

1456
00:55:42,292 --> 00:55:43,462
and cheese baguette.

1457
00:55:44,932 --> 00:55:46,692
(This time, he'll have salty types of bread.)

1458
00:55:48,602 --> 00:55:50,702
- Does it not feel greasy? - No.

1459
00:55:51,532 --> 00:55:53,532
He must handle greasy food well.

1460
00:55:56,102 --> 00:55:58,111
I'm seeing all kinds of bread I've never seen before.

1461
00:55:58,112 --> 00:55:59,342
I've never seen those as well.

1462
00:56:00,042 --> 00:56:02,512
- That's Emmental cheese. - That looks amazing!

1463
00:56:03,612 --> 00:56:05,052
You've given up on low-sugar food all of sudden.

1464
00:56:06,312 --> 00:56:07,451
He had low-sugar food...

1465
00:56:07,452 --> 00:56:08,581
- to have all of the bread. - Right!

1466
00:56:08,582 --> 00:56:10,181
- That will definitely be fattening. - It's his cheat day.

1467
00:56:10,182 --> 00:56:11,221
It was my half-cheat day.

1468
00:56:11,222 --> 00:56:12,292
What did you have when you were on a diet?

1469
00:56:12,352 --> 00:56:14,421
There's a bread that's made of protein.

1470
00:56:14,422 --> 00:56:16,191
- Protein bread? - Right. That's a thing.

1471
00:56:16,192 --> 00:56:17,192
Protein bread?

1472
00:56:17,193 --> 00:56:18,731
- So. - There are protein chocolate pies.

1473
00:56:18,732 --> 00:56:20,232
I couldn't give up on having bread.

1474
00:56:23,832 --> 00:56:24,832
(Crunchy)

1475
00:56:27,972 --> 00:56:29,272
(Satisfied)

1476
00:56:29,872 --> 00:56:31,211
(He moves around as it's delicious.)

1477
00:56:31,212 --> 00:56:32,372
That must be the best one.

1478
00:56:33,072 --> 00:56:34,212
Gosh, I want some.

1479
00:56:34,882 --> 00:56:36,542
I love Emmental bagels as well.

1480
00:56:38,152 --> 00:56:41,012
As I had something salty, I'll have something sweet.

1481
00:56:42,852 --> 00:56:44,992
I want some kimchi jjigae just after watching this.

1482
00:56:48,392 --> 00:56:50,622
- Gosh, that looks good too. - Is that garlic bread?

1483
00:56:50,922 --> 00:56:52,291
That's the cheddar cheese baguette.

1484
00:56:52,292 --> 00:56:53,792
He's having more cheese than a European.

1485
00:56:56,462 --> 00:56:58,102
He ate bread for an hour.

1486
00:56:59,572 --> 00:57:01,742
(He cleans up again.)

1487
00:57:03,102 --> 00:57:05,342
(I'm done with the cleaning.)

1488
00:57:07,272 --> 00:57:09,482
(He washes the dishrag right away as well.)

1489
00:57:13,212 --> 00:57:14,312
That's neat.

1490
00:57:19,222 --> 00:57:20,892
(An exercise bike?)

1491
00:57:22,022 --> 00:57:23,362
(He even gets changed.)

1492
00:57:29,562 --> 00:57:32,272
(He starts exercising right after having breakfast at 8am.)

1493
00:57:35,202 --> 00:57:37,971
Doesn't the food come up...

1494
00:57:37,972 --> 00:57:39,512
if you ride that right after eating?

1495
00:57:39,712 --> 00:57:42,482
I used the exercise bike every single day.

1496
00:57:42,612 --> 00:57:45,682
I've tried using it before my meals and after my meals.

1497
00:57:46,082 --> 00:57:47,412
It suited me better to use it after meals.

1498
00:57:47,552 --> 00:57:49,521
It felt like it burned and digested away...

1499
00:57:49,522 --> 00:57:51,392
the food that I had.

1500
00:57:52,692 --> 00:57:55,322
(It has been 6 minutes since he started pedaling.)

1501
00:57:56,022 --> 00:57:57,291
(Sweating)

1502
00:57:57,292 --> 00:57:59,092
- He sweats a lot. - His sweating is coming out.

1503
00:58:01,332 --> 00:58:03,201
(He wraps his head with the towel...)

1504
00:58:03,202 --> 00:58:05,272
(and starts pedaling even faster.)

1505
00:58:06,702 --> 00:58:08,602
- There's the cheese coming out. - Cheese?

1506
00:58:09,402 --> 00:58:10,972
That was the cream just now.

1507
00:58:11,472 --> 00:58:12,642
The Emmental cheese.

1508
00:58:16,712 --> 00:58:20,252
(He moves his body to digest the bread he had.)

1509
00:58:23,222 --> 00:58:24,452
(Dripping)

1510
00:58:26,152 --> 00:58:27,152
(Grunting)

1511
00:58:29,192 --> 00:58:32,191
(This morning...)

1512
00:58:32,192 --> 00:58:33,292
That's tough to do.

1513
00:58:34,292 --> 00:58:35,402
I can't do that.

1514
00:58:36,932 --> 00:58:38,102
Gosh.

1515
00:58:38,702 --> 00:58:40,502
- How many calories is that? - Around 175?

1516
00:58:43,902 --> 00:58:45,712
(Picking up)

1517
00:58:50,812 --> 00:58:52,082
Don't tell me he's ordering bread.

1518
00:58:53,382 --> 00:58:54,482
An order for bread.

1519
00:58:54,982 --> 00:58:57,482
- Seo Bum June! - What are you up to, Grandma?

1520
00:58:57,622 --> 00:58:59,391
- It's your grandmother? - Yes.

1521
00:58:59,392 --> 00:59:01,522
I was taking out the trash to prepare to move out.

1522
00:59:02,192 --> 00:59:03,722
I should've gone to help you.

1523
00:59:04,062 --> 00:59:06,791
Gosh, you're too busy. Why bother?

1524
00:59:06,792 --> 00:59:08,302
I'm not busy.

1525
00:59:08,462 --> 00:59:09,901
- Grandma. - Yes?

1526
00:59:09,902 --> 00:59:11,161
After moving into the new house and getting things sorted,

1527
00:59:11,162 --> 00:59:13,572
you have to take a picture with me as you promised to.

1528
00:59:14,002 --> 00:59:15,841
- Sure. - She has a great grandson.

1529
00:59:15,842 --> 00:59:17,802
- Okay. - All right.

1530
00:59:18,042 --> 00:59:19,312
I love you, Grandma.

1531
00:59:19,512 --> 00:59:21,211
- I love you too. - I miss my grandmother!

1532
00:59:21,212 --> 00:59:22,242
Bye.

1533
00:59:23,182 --> 00:59:25,412
(He carried on with his exercise with his grandmother's support.)

1534
00:59:25,682 --> 00:59:27,581
(I've given it my all.)

1535
00:59:27,582 --> 00:59:28,652
Done.

1536
00:59:30,522 --> 00:59:32,822
(He completes his 51-minute morning exercise.)

1537
00:59:35,392 --> 00:59:36,821
Gosh, look at how his back is drenched.

1538
00:59:36,822 --> 00:59:38,131
It's great to sweat in the morning.

1539
00:59:38,132 --> 00:59:39,932
- Right. - It must feel relieving.

1540
00:59:44,262 --> 00:59:46,702
(He takes a refreshing shower after sweating.)

1541
00:59:48,002 --> 00:59:49,372
I'll be back.

1542
00:59:57,982 --> 00:59:59,352
Where is he going this early?

1543
00:59:59,512 --> 01:00:00,982
He left the house at 9am.

1544
01:00:07,592 --> 01:00:09,362
Let's go.

1545
01:00:11,862 --> 01:00:12,962
Where could he be going?

1546
01:00:15,702 --> 01:00:16,961
Isn't it a department store?

1547
01:00:16,962 --> 01:00:19,102
It feels like a shopping center.

1548
01:00:21,002 --> 01:00:22,102
Where is this?

1549
01:00:27,572 --> 01:00:28,982
- It's a bakery. - Are you serious?

1550
01:00:29,082 --> 01:00:30,912
- Seriously? - No way!

1551
01:00:31,852 --> 01:00:33,482
(Injeolmi butter, peanut butter chocolate chip bar)

1552
01:00:34,182 --> 01:00:36,422
(The counter is filled with various types of desserts.)

1553
01:00:37,282 --> 01:00:40,521
(Bum June heads straight to the kitchen.)

1554
01:00:40,522 --> 01:00:41,892
- What? - You run a bakery?

1555
01:00:41,992 --> 01:00:43,162
(Chuckling)

1556
01:00:44,122 --> 01:00:47,461
(He heads to the kitchen right after entering.)

1557
01:00:47,462 --> 01:00:48,832
- What? - You run a bakery?

1558
01:00:50,262 --> 01:00:52,371
It must be so that he can have a lot of bread.

1559
01:00:52,372 --> 01:00:53,831
Is that why he works at a bakery?

1560
01:00:53,832 --> 01:00:54,971
- As a part-timer? - Yes.

1561
01:00:54,972 --> 01:00:56,742
You must be paid with bread.

1562
01:00:58,642 --> 01:01:01,042
(He starts the coffee machine like a skilled part-timer.)

1563
01:01:04,382 --> 01:01:06,981
(He makes two cups of iced Americano in a flash.)

1564
01:01:06,982 --> 01:01:08,051
- Gosh. - Who is that?

1565
01:01:08,052 --> 01:01:09,222
It's the owner.

1566
01:01:09,852 --> 01:01:11,152
- Hey, sis. - Yes?

1567
01:01:12,052 --> 01:01:13,492
I'll help you now. Tell me what to do.

1568
01:01:14,152 --> 01:01:18,021
This is the dessert cafe...

1569
01:01:18,022 --> 01:01:19,791
that my older sister runs.

1570
01:01:19,792 --> 01:01:20,931
- I see. - I see.

1571
01:01:20,932 --> 01:01:23,261
At times, during my days off,

1572
01:01:23,262 --> 01:01:25,632
I work as a part-timer at my sister's store.

1573
01:01:25,732 --> 01:01:29,071
I was told there was a big order for 700 butter bars.

1574
01:01:29,072 --> 01:01:30,902
- An order for 700 butter bars? - That was why I came to help.

1575
01:01:32,412 --> 01:01:33,672
So those are butter bars?

1576
01:01:34,242 --> 01:01:35,312
They're soft.

1577
01:01:35,712 --> 01:01:37,481
Each box must have 74 butter bars.

1578
01:01:37,482 --> 01:01:39,111
There are 74 in 1? Okay.

1579
01:01:39,112 --> 01:01:40,451
You can start with this.

1580
01:01:40,452 --> 01:01:42,122
(I got it.)

1581
01:01:42,852 --> 01:01:45,792
(Focused)

1582
01:01:49,222 --> 01:01:51,832
(The basket is emptied in no time.)

1583
01:01:51,992 --> 01:01:53,862
- Another box. - Okay.

1584
01:01:56,702 --> 01:01:58,102
Is she making the butter bars back there?

1585
01:01:58,232 --> 01:01:59,972
Yes. She kept making them.

1586
01:02:05,472 --> 01:02:07,641
(The younger brother focuses on packaging them.)

1587
01:02:07,642 --> 01:02:09,212
It looks like he has done this many times before.

1588
01:02:11,312 --> 01:02:12,381
Wait for me.

1589
01:02:12,382 --> 01:02:14,412
(Another box is filled in a short period of time.)

1590
01:02:14,652 --> 01:02:15,782
It's quite heavy.

1591
01:02:17,582 --> 01:02:19,551
It shows that he has worked as a part-timer for quite some time.

1592
01:02:19,552 --> 01:02:21,422
- He knows how to work. - He knows how to work.

1593
01:02:23,062 --> 01:02:24,931
Deal with the order as well.

1594
01:02:24,932 --> 01:02:25,992
The order?

1595
01:02:26,562 --> 01:02:28,702
(Walking over)

1596
01:02:30,632 --> 01:02:32,972
(He checks the order right away.)

1597
01:02:34,202 --> 01:02:35,472
Vanilla pound.

1598
01:02:36,288 --> 01:02:37,488
Strawberry butter bar.

1599
01:02:38,872 --> 01:02:41,942
(He finds the desserts skillfully.)

1600
01:02:43,412 --> 01:02:45,582
(Stooping)

1601
01:02:45,812 --> 01:02:48,422
(Scribbling)

1602
01:02:48,722 --> 01:02:50,752
(He writes the note himself this time.)

1603
01:02:51,752 --> 01:02:52,952
Gosh, his handwriting is so nice.

1604
01:02:53,692 --> 01:02:54,751
Your handwriting makes my heart flutter.

1605
01:02:54,752 --> 01:02:56,262
It's like that of a high school girl.

1606
01:02:58,562 --> 01:03:00,991
You see that kind of handwriting from the notebook of a girl...

1607
01:03:00,992 --> 01:03:02,131
who receives good grades.

1608
01:03:02,132 --> 01:03:03,702
- That... - Those who write diaries well.

1609
01:03:04,402 --> 01:03:05,801
If a note with that handwriting is stuck on a canned coffee...

1610
01:03:05,802 --> 01:03:06,832
and placed on my desk...

1611
01:03:07,132 --> 01:03:08,242
"What is this?"

1612
01:03:08,942 --> 01:03:11,001
But it'd say, "Please keep quiet."

1613
01:03:11,002 --> 01:03:12,271
(Breaking the fantasy)

1614
01:03:12,272 --> 01:03:13,911
Bum June would've written it.

1615
01:03:13,912 --> 01:03:14,912
(Please keep quiet.)

1616
01:03:15,342 --> 01:03:17,882
(Writing a note that shook Kian84's heart)

1617
01:03:18,912 --> 01:03:21,652
(Sticking it on the bag)

1618
01:03:22,222 --> 01:03:24,822
(Focused)

1619
01:03:25,722 --> 01:03:27,721
Gosh, he's good.

1620
01:03:27,722 --> 01:03:29,222
Goodness, he's meticulous.

1621
01:03:29,492 --> 01:03:31,662
(A one-day partner who does his job skillfully)

1622
01:03:32,492 --> 01:03:33,992
I've worked part time at a cafe...

1623
01:03:34,192 --> 01:03:35,632
and a bar.

1624
01:03:36,502 --> 01:03:38,002
I've even worked part time at an internet cafe too.

1625
01:03:38,602 --> 01:03:40,832
While working part time,

1626
01:03:41,132 --> 01:03:44,401
- I saw Yoo Ji Tae. - I think I saw that video.

1627
01:03:44,402 --> 01:03:46,842
I think I was 20 then.

1628
01:03:46,912 --> 01:03:48,912
- I actually saw this. - What is this?

1629
01:03:49,112 --> 01:03:50,782
- What is this? - What is it?

1630
01:03:51,982 --> 01:03:53,751
(9 years ago, Bum June was working part time,)

1631
01:03:53,752 --> 01:03:55,522
(dreaming of becoming an actor.)

1632
01:04:00,692 --> 01:04:02,822
(Hi, Bum June.)

1633
01:04:03,522 --> 01:04:04,821
(His role model Yoo Ji Tae visited him at his part time work.)

1634
01:04:04,822 --> 01:04:06,491
(Teary-eyed)

1635
01:04:06,492 --> 01:04:08,302
I'm Yoo Ji Tae.

1636
01:04:09,102 --> 01:04:11,001
This itself looks like a drama.

1637
01:04:11,002 --> 01:04:12,972
I know. It looks like a setup, right?

1638
01:04:13,472 --> 01:04:17,142
I heard that they were filming a documentary...

1639
01:04:17,302 --> 01:04:19,812
about people who do many part-time jobs.

1640
01:04:20,112 --> 01:04:21,471
- The crew lied to you. - Yes.

1641
01:04:21,472 --> 01:04:22,882
They told me it was a documentary.

1642
01:04:22,942 --> 01:04:26,381
To root for a student who dreams of becoming an actor,

1643
01:04:26,382 --> 01:04:27,951
Ji Tae went there.

1644
01:04:27,952 --> 01:04:29,751
- Really? - Because his role model was Ji Tae.

1645
01:04:29,752 --> 01:04:31,251
- Oh, from that channel? - Yes.

1646
01:04:31,252 --> 01:04:32,891
There was a lot of similar content back then.

1647
01:04:32,892 --> 01:04:34,752
- It must've been really moving. - It must've been really moving.

1648
01:04:35,062 --> 01:04:37,161
(Take a seat.)

1649
01:04:37,162 --> 01:04:39,262
(Let's have a beer together.)

1650
01:04:39,462 --> 01:04:40,862
- I heard you studied acting. - Yes.

1651
01:04:40,992 --> 01:04:44,202
(I came to see you.)

1652
01:04:44,962 --> 01:04:50,172
(Yoo Ji Tae gave heartfelt advice without holding back.)

1653
01:04:50,902 --> 01:04:53,341
I wanted to see him after that,

1654
01:04:53,342 --> 01:04:55,142
and I saw him at a movie premier.

1655
01:04:55,382 --> 01:04:56,582
- After you made it? - Yes.

1656
01:04:57,582 --> 01:04:59,311
I said hello to him then,

1657
01:04:59,312 --> 01:05:00,981
- and he remembered me. - Of course.

1658
01:05:00,982 --> 01:05:04,582
- Of course he remembers. - We exchanged our numbers then.

1659
01:05:05,222 --> 01:05:07,392
I still keep in touch with him.

1660
01:05:09,322 --> 01:05:10,522
- I see. - He's like a savior.

1661
01:05:11,522 --> 01:05:14,462
Why was Yoo Ji Tae your role model among many actors?

1662
01:05:14,632 --> 01:05:18,232
I came to like him after seeing one of his interviews.

1663
01:05:18,302 --> 01:05:21,032
Like the things he told me.

1664
01:05:21,572 --> 01:05:24,342
When I heard that in person...

1665
01:05:25,772 --> 01:05:29,081
Even now, I get emotional thinking about it.

1666
01:05:29,082 --> 01:05:30,481
(He becomes emotional even now.)

1667
01:05:30,482 --> 01:05:31,541
I don't think I can even talk to him.

1668
01:05:31,542 --> 01:05:32,612
My goodness.

1669
01:05:33,282 --> 01:05:35,222
- I see. - My gosh.

1670
01:05:36,122 --> 01:05:39,322
(A 20-year-old young man who dreamed of becoming an actor...)

1671
01:05:39,592 --> 01:05:43,722
(grew into an actor who won all the Best Rookie Awards.)

1672
01:05:44,262 --> 01:05:47,991
I was really happy, and it was a really precious moment.

1673
01:05:47,992 --> 01:05:49,662
It must've motivated you big time.

1674
01:05:54,532 --> 01:05:56,742
- Hey. I'll take the order. - Okay.

1675
01:05:57,742 --> 01:06:00,412
(Packing for the delivery orders skillfully)

1676
01:06:01,112 --> 01:06:03,512
One yellow cheese pudding and one yellow cheese crumble?

1677
01:06:04,212 --> 01:06:06,412
I'll leave the two cups of coffee here.

1678
01:06:08,012 --> 01:06:10,482
Your sister must trust you a lot and leave it to you.

1679
01:06:10,622 --> 01:06:12,051
Of course. It's the best...

1680
01:06:12,052 --> 01:06:13,492
- when your family works for you. - Mission clear.

1681
01:06:15,122 --> 01:06:18,121
(Packing even the last box neatly)

1682
01:06:18,122 --> 01:06:19,661
(Same-day delivery, fresh food)

1683
01:06:19,662 --> 01:06:20,961
Gosh, 700 butter bars?

1684
01:06:20,962 --> 01:06:23,831
(They finally finished packing 700 butter bars.)

1685
01:06:23,832 --> 01:06:24,832
You're the best.

1686
01:06:25,432 --> 01:06:27,902
Great job. Thank you so much.

1687
01:06:28,402 --> 01:06:29,742
- Are we done? - Yes, we are.

1688
01:06:29,942 --> 01:06:31,042
We are?

1689
01:06:31,772 --> 01:06:34,412
I'll take one apple banana strawberry crumble.

1690
01:06:34,742 --> 01:06:36,011
Apple banana strawberry crumble sounds good.

1691
01:06:36,012 --> 01:06:37,141
One pumpkin pie.

1692
01:06:37,142 --> 01:06:38,852
(One pumpkin pie, please.)

1693
01:06:39,352 --> 01:06:40,411
(Picking as much bread as he can to satisfy a sweet craving)

1694
01:06:40,412 --> 01:06:41,822
It's salt and butter.

1695
01:06:42,252 --> 01:06:43,252
He loves bread so much.

1696
01:06:43,253 --> 01:06:45,221
It was urgent, and you helped me today,

1697
01:06:45,222 --> 01:06:46,592
so I'll give them to you for free.

1698
01:06:47,452 --> 01:06:49,462
Because I love bread, she gives me bread...

1699
01:06:49,692 --> 01:06:51,321
for my labor.

1700
01:06:51,322 --> 01:06:52,431
- For your labor? - Yes.

1701
01:06:52,432 --> 01:06:54,831
For your sister, there won't be any leftover bread.

1702
01:06:54,832 --> 01:06:56,501
- It'd be nice. - She'd be grateful.

1703
01:06:56,502 --> 01:06:57,631
Because it's iffy to sell it if there's only one day left...

1704
01:06:57,632 --> 01:06:58,731
until the expiration date.

1705
01:06:58,732 --> 01:07:00,402
- They throw away all the leftovers. - Yes.

1706
01:07:00,672 --> 01:07:02,601
- You're such a nice brother. - Of course.

1707
01:07:02,602 --> 01:07:03,741
- It's really nice. - She gets to clear the leftovers...

1708
01:07:03,742 --> 01:07:04,871
- and save money for your labor. - She doesn't have to throw them.

1709
01:07:04,872 --> 01:07:07,342
I hope my brother who's in Gwangju watches this.

1710
01:07:10,212 --> 01:07:11,412
You should heat it up before eating it.

1711
01:07:13,352 --> 01:07:15,821
- It looks so good. It's insane. - You should heat it up.

1712
01:07:15,822 --> 01:07:17,151
- On top of this... You know, right? - He's so sweet.

1713
01:07:17,152 --> 01:07:18,251
Add that.

1714
01:07:18,252 --> 01:07:20,292
- Okay. - A brother does that?

1715
01:07:20,422 --> 01:07:21,752
This is impossible.

1716
01:07:22,222 --> 01:07:23,362
Thanks for this.

1717
01:07:23,792 --> 01:07:25,962
- Thank you for the food too. - Thank you.

1718
01:07:26,762 --> 01:07:27,832
I'll get going.

1719
01:07:28,832 --> 01:07:30,402
- Bye. - This is so lovely to watch.

1720
01:07:31,002 --> 01:07:32,172
Great work today.

1721
01:07:32,302 --> 01:07:34,472
He'll get even closer to her as he gets older.

1722
01:07:34,632 --> 01:07:36,071
There are siblings like them.

1723
01:07:36,072 --> 01:07:37,072
(Thanks to his sister, he packed lots of bread.)

1724
01:07:38,242 --> 01:07:41,212
(Going back home where Monde is waiting)

1725
01:07:44,112 --> 01:07:45,282
Monde.

1726
01:07:45,682 --> 01:07:47,751
Monde, you waited for me?

1727
01:07:47,752 --> 01:07:48,821
Gosh, he must've waited for you.

1728
01:07:48,822 --> 01:07:50,481
Goodness.

1729
01:07:50,482 --> 01:07:51,851
You're so cute.

1730
01:07:51,852 --> 01:07:53,851
- Monde, you're so cute. - He wants to play with him.

1731
01:07:53,852 --> 01:07:55,491
Goodness. There.

1732
01:07:55,492 --> 01:07:58,062
I see. You missed me.

1733
01:07:58,422 --> 01:08:00,392
- Gosh, he was bored. - I love it.

1734
01:08:01,032 --> 01:08:02,801
Monde, did you miss me?

1735
01:08:02,802 --> 01:08:04,462
Gosh. Did you sleep well?

1736
01:08:05,232 --> 01:08:06,732
(Opening)

1737
01:08:08,102 --> 01:08:09,242
The food supply.

1738
01:08:09,442 --> 01:08:10,502
Bread freezer.

1739
01:08:11,672 --> 01:08:13,612
He eats and refills.

1740
01:08:15,542 --> 01:08:17,541
I should eat now too, right?

1741
01:08:17,542 --> 01:08:19,382
Oh, it's only 1pm.

1742
01:08:20,512 --> 01:08:23,252
(He naturally heads to the fridge.)

1743
01:08:23,752 --> 01:08:24,951
I was starving.

1744
01:08:24,952 --> 01:08:27,552
- It was past lunchtime. - Have some rice, please.

1745
01:08:28,962 --> 01:08:30,322
(Opening)

1746
01:08:31,392 --> 01:08:33,661
(He took out red kimchi that has aged well.)

1747
01:08:33,662 --> 01:08:34,662
There you go.

1748
01:08:37,732 --> 01:08:39,771
(In the pan coated with oil,)

1749
01:08:39,772 --> 01:08:41,332
(he makes scallion oil.)

1750
01:08:41,872 --> 01:08:44,242
I used chicken breast ham to feel less guilty.

1751
01:08:45,512 --> 01:08:48,312
(Then he fries spicy kimchi on top of it.)

1752
01:08:49,212 --> 01:08:50,481
(Pouring)

1753
01:08:50,482 --> 01:08:51,682
Oh, is it kimchi fried rice?

1754
01:08:52,382 --> 01:08:54,382
Gosh, I love that.

1755
01:08:54,912 --> 01:08:56,022
It looks so good.

1756
01:08:58,592 --> 01:09:00,422
(Focused)

1757
01:09:02,362 --> 01:09:03,362
What?

1758
01:09:03,363 --> 01:09:04,391
(Making a hole in the middle?)

1759
01:09:04,392 --> 01:09:05,732
- Eggs. - He must be adding eggs.

1760
01:09:09,032 --> 01:09:10,102
Eggs or...

1761
01:09:11,432 --> 01:09:12,771
It's cream. It's whipping cream.

1762
01:09:12,772 --> 01:09:13,931
Gosh, whipping cream?

1763
01:09:13,932 --> 01:09:15,871
- Is it risotto? - To that precious kimchi...

1764
01:09:15,872 --> 01:09:17,802
(They can't imagine the taste.)

1765
01:09:18,402 --> 01:09:21,012
Today, I chose kimchi fried rice.

1766
01:09:21,672 --> 01:09:24,412
It's cheddar, mozzarella, whipping cream kimchi fried rice.

1767
01:09:25,082 --> 01:09:27,911
I first saw the recipe on social media.

1768
01:09:27,912 --> 01:09:29,352
I was really curious how it'd taste.

1769
01:09:30,922 --> 01:09:33,352
(Shall I make it in earnest?)

1770
01:09:34,492 --> 01:09:36,722
Add mozzarella and cheddar cheese.

1771
01:09:36,892 --> 01:09:38,492
Then add a slice of cheddar cheese.

1772
01:09:38,662 --> 01:09:40,491
Then close the lid and melt them.

1773
01:09:40,492 --> 01:09:44,162
Then it becomes kimchi fried rice...

1774
01:09:44,802 --> 01:09:47,002
that's like thick and creamy risotto.

1775
01:09:48,072 --> 01:09:50,572
- Oh, like rose style? - Yes, like risotto.

1776
01:09:50,742 --> 01:09:52,211
It must be.

1777
01:09:52,212 --> 01:09:53,541
You must like Western food.

1778
01:09:53,542 --> 01:09:56,381
Yes, I like cheese and dairy products.

1779
01:09:56,382 --> 01:09:57,612
(It's a perfect dish for a cheese lover.)

1780
01:09:58,342 --> 01:09:59,512
It's done.

1781
01:10:01,852 --> 01:10:04,682
(Carrying the whole pot)

1782
01:10:07,422 --> 01:10:08,662
Goodness.

1783
01:10:08,822 --> 01:10:09,822
What is it?

1784
01:10:10,362 --> 01:10:12,961
(Kimchi fried rice that's like risotto is ready.)

1785
01:10:12,962 --> 01:10:14,662
(Exclaiming)

1786
01:10:16,162 --> 01:10:18,332
(It looks a bit unfamiliar.)

1787
01:10:19,302 --> 01:10:21,602
(He mixes it thoroughly.)

1788
01:10:23,002 --> 01:10:25,741
(Cheese stretching)

1789
01:10:25,742 --> 01:10:27,112
The cheese looks so good.

1790
01:10:28,412 --> 01:10:30,942
(Taking a bite)

1791
01:10:32,852 --> 01:10:34,682
(Amazed)

1792
01:10:37,022 --> 01:10:38,081
(Exclaiming)

1793
01:10:38,082 --> 01:10:39,452
(Enjoying)

1794
01:10:39,692 --> 01:10:40,752
This is crazy.

1795
01:10:41,792 --> 01:10:44,362
It tastes exactly like risotto.

1796
01:10:45,162 --> 01:10:47,531
It wraps the kimchi fried rice smoothly.

1797
01:10:47,532 --> 01:10:49,632
I'd like to try a bite.

1798
01:10:50,902 --> 01:10:53,172
