2055
01:21:17,922 --> 01:21:20,831
Ma'am, I'll take a plate of baby crab.

2056
01:21:20,832 --> 01:21:22,592
That's delicious. I like that.

2057
01:21:22,962 --> 01:21:24,731
You just pressed it?

2058
01:21:24,732 --> 01:21:26,431
Gosh, thank you.

2059
01:21:26,432 --> 01:21:27,572
(He picks up the packed yellowtail.)

2060
01:21:28,432 --> 01:21:29,541
Monde, let's go now.

2061
01:21:29,542 --> 01:21:31,342
(He returns home with both hands full.)

2062
01:21:34,142 --> 01:21:35,742
(He got a lot of things.)

2063
01:21:38,082 --> 01:21:42,352
(Washing his hands thoroughly as soon as he comes home)

2064
01:21:43,322 --> 01:21:45,151
(He gets ready to eat.)

2065
01:21:45,152 --> 01:21:46,222
Goodness.

2066
01:21:48,052 --> 01:21:49,091
My gosh.

2067
01:21:49,092 --> 01:21:51,522
(Putting the fritters together)

2068
01:21:53,262 --> 01:21:54,492
This is crazy.

2069
01:21:56,932 --> 01:21:58,231
This is crazy.

2070
01:21:58,232 --> 01:21:59,472
- Yellowtail looks crazy good. - Gosh, that looks delicious.

2071
01:21:59,572 --> 01:22:01,231
He cut it thick.

2072
01:22:01,232 --> 01:22:02,802
You need to cut yellowtail thick.

2073
01:22:03,572 --> 01:22:06,711
(Putting the vegetables and white kimchi neatly on a dish)

2074
01:22:06,712 --> 01:22:08,911
That's what makes you happy. Spreading food and eating it.

2075
01:22:08,912 --> 01:22:10,682
That's why you work hard.

2076
01:22:11,012 --> 01:22:12,811
(A table filled with food from the traditional market)

2077
01:22:12,812 --> 01:22:15,452
Isn't that too much to eat by yourself?

2078
01:22:15,682 --> 01:22:17,482
I held back a lot while I was on a diet.

2079
01:22:17,822 --> 01:22:18,881
Monde.

2080
01:22:18,882 --> 01:22:19,991
(Lights off)

2081
01:22:19,992 --> 01:22:21,091
He's setting the mood.

2082
01:22:21,092 --> 01:22:22,962
That's when I'm the happiest.

2083
01:22:25,122 --> 01:22:26,191
Thank you for the food.

2084
01:22:26,192 --> 01:22:27,432
(Solemn)

2085
01:22:28,092 --> 01:22:29,161
For the first bite...

2086
01:22:29,162 --> 01:22:30,532
(Salivating)

2087
01:22:31,732 --> 01:22:33,001
The yellowtail looks good.

2088
01:22:33,002 --> 01:22:35,202
(Taking a piece of thick yellowtail)

2089
01:22:35,802 --> 01:22:37,241
(Dipping it in salt...)

2090
01:22:37,242 --> 01:22:39,302
(then in sesame oil)

2091
01:22:43,182 --> 01:22:44,581
The yellowtail from that store was really good.

2092
01:22:44,582 --> 01:22:45,711
(Smiling)

2093
01:22:45,712 --> 01:22:46,812
I love it.

2094
01:22:48,282 --> 01:22:50,052
It's therapeutic for me to see you not having bread.

2095
01:22:54,222 --> 01:22:55,922
Since I'm having yellowtail by myself...

2096
01:22:56,052 --> 01:22:57,092
He's having two pieces at once.

2097
01:22:58,262 --> 01:23:00,332
- Add aged kimchi on top. - Aged kimchi sounds good.

2098
01:23:03,562 --> 01:23:05,132
This adds a kick to it. And add sesame oil.

2099
01:23:06,202 --> 01:23:08,572
(Adding pickled chili and wasabi that'll make it less greasy)

2100
01:23:10,602 --> 01:23:11,901
My goodness. Yellowtail.

2101
01:23:11,902 --> 01:23:13,541
That combination is really good.

2102
01:23:13,542 --> 01:23:15,672
- I know. - I love it.

2103
01:23:16,182 --> 01:23:17,711
You should have a fully grown yellowtail.

2104
01:23:17,712 --> 01:23:19,582
(A taste that makes you laugh)

2105
01:23:20,612 --> 01:23:22,712
(Getting up)

2106
01:23:24,152 --> 01:23:26,822
(Opening the fridge in the middle of his meal)

2107
01:23:28,822 --> 01:23:30,521
(Adding a huge ice cube)

2108
01:23:30,522 --> 01:23:31,921
- That's it. - Take your time.

2109
01:23:31,922 --> 01:23:33,462
- Do you drink too? - I love it.

2110
01:23:35,692 --> 01:23:37,732
(Filling the cool iced cup)

2111
01:23:38,032 --> 01:23:39,932
It looks like you're at an izakaya.

2112
01:23:40,032 --> 01:23:42,171
- That's right. - You should finish it in two sips.

2113
01:23:42,172 --> 01:23:43,401
The small glass won't do.

2114
01:23:43,402 --> 01:23:45,042
- Let all the organs feel it. - I know.

2115
01:23:45,172 --> 01:23:47,112
You finally talk now that he's having soju.

2116
01:23:47,972 --> 01:23:49,882
(Gulping)

2117
01:23:51,382 --> 01:23:53,451
Your health is okay, right? Is your cholesterol level okay?

2118
01:23:53,452 --> 01:23:54,852
Yes, I have clean blood.

2119
01:23:55,082 --> 01:23:56,981
I work out as much as I eat.

2120
01:23:56,982 --> 01:23:58,852
You must work out hard.

2121
01:23:59,052 --> 01:24:01,152
- I really love that. - I know.

2122
01:24:01,992 --> 01:24:03,322
(Crunchy)

2123
01:24:03,892 --> 01:24:06,432
(Frowning as it's so good)

2124
01:24:06,562 --> 01:24:10,462
Thanks to today, I think I can keep going forward.

2125
01:24:12,132 --> 01:24:15,272
I got to think that it's good to eat...

2126
01:24:15,502 --> 01:24:19,642
when my body craves it. I think it's good for my body.

2127
01:24:19,912 --> 01:24:21,872
You hold back your desires to eat on other days.

2128
01:24:22,412 --> 01:24:23,942
I need to watch my figure my whole life.

2129
01:24:24,012 --> 01:24:28,451
Because I want to be an actor all my life,

2130
01:24:28,452 --> 01:24:30,722
I need to have a healthy mentality...

2131
01:24:30,952 --> 01:24:32,581
and eat when I want to.

2132
01:24:32,582 --> 01:24:34,192
Then I'll move around more.

2133
01:24:34,552 --> 01:24:36,422
I think this kind of mindset is important.

2134
01:24:38,292 --> 01:24:39,392
It's so good.

2135
01:24:41,032 --> 01:24:43,662
(The cheat day he hasn't had for a while is ending.)

2136
01:24:45,102 --> 01:24:46,772
- What is this? - Bread again?

2137
01:24:49,302 --> 01:24:50,701
(Amazed)

2138
01:24:50,702 --> 01:24:51,941
What is that?

2139
01:24:51,942 --> 01:24:53,171
- What is that? - It's cheese on carp bread.

2140
01:24:53,172 --> 01:24:54,372
- No, I mean butter. - Butter on carp bread.

2141
01:24:55,472 --> 01:24:56,812
It was really good.

2142
01:24:57,112 --> 01:24:58,112
Gosh.

2143
01:24:58,113 --> 01:24:59,512
Then he'll ride the indoor bike again.

2144
01:25:00,112 --> 01:25:01,282
He should.

2145
01:25:01,952 --> 01:25:05,252
(Cheat Day Filled with Happiness is Over)

2146
01:25:05,852 --> 01:25:07,292
(Next story)

2147
01:25:08,322 --> 01:25:12,022
(Feeling nervous amid the murmuring)

2148
01:25:12,122 --> 01:25:13,562
(Hyun Moo is standing in the middle of it.)

2149
01:25:14,362 --> 01:25:16,362
(It's a wedding hall?)

2150
01:25:17,102 --> 01:25:18,962
(May I ask you to officiate my wedding?)

2151
01:25:19,362 --> 01:25:20,972
(Officiate a wedding when I'm not married?)

2152
01:25:21,572 --> 01:25:22,572
(Kian84 will host the wedding.)

2153
01:25:22,573 --> 01:25:23,902
(Moomoo will officiate the wedding.)

2154
01:25:23,972 --> 01:25:25,102
(Soon to debut as an officiator)

2155
01:25:25,902 --> 01:25:27,212
(Stammering)

2156
01:25:27,842 --> 01:25:29,682
(Can you host it if I fail to?)

2157
01:25:30,482 --> 01:25:31,882
(I'm serious.)

2158
01:25:32,842 --> 01:25:35,652
(I'm in no position to help.)

2159
01:25:37,052 --> 01:25:38,421
(The wedding hall is packed with people,)

2160
01:25:38,422 --> 01:25:40,352
(making him even more nervous.)

2161
01:25:41,452 --> 01:25:42,552
(Jang Woo)

2162
01:25:42,922 --> 01:25:44,322
(Finally meeting the star of the day)

2163
01:25:45,092 --> 01:25:46,932
(Hyun Moo, I'm counting on you.)

2164
01:25:48,062 --> 01:25:49,801
(Host84 is heading to the stage.)

2165
01:25:49,802 --> 01:25:51,002
(Where does an officiator sit?)

2166
01:25:51,532 --> 01:25:53,672
(It's my first time officiating. Will I be able to do well?)

2167
01:25:54,032 --> 01:25:55,071
(This is nothing.)

2168
01:25:55,072 --> 01:25:56,442
(Yes, Hyun Moo. Let's do this.)

2169
01:25:57,802 --> 01:26:00,412
(Soon, the wedding begins.)

2170
01:26:00,972 --> 01:26:02,211
(Please welcome Mr. Jun Hyun Moo...)

2171
01:26:02,212 --> 01:26:05,042
(with a round of applause.)

2172
01:26:06,852 --> 01:26:08,212
(He's the star of the wedding.)

2173
01:26:09,082 --> 01:26:11,081
(Groom Lee Jang Woo...)

2174
01:26:11,082 --> 01:26:13,792
(enters.)

2175
01:26:14,692 --> 01:26:16,321
(Here comes Jang Woo.)

2176
01:26:16,322 --> 01:26:17,462
(He must be nervous. Oh, gosh.)

2177
01:26:18,022 --> 01:26:19,992
(The Rainbow Club members are nervous as well.)

2178
01:26:21,532 --> 01:26:23,762
(Palm Oil Prince Jang Woo is about to say goodbye.)

2179
01:26:25,332 --> 01:26:32,302
(Goodbye will hurt us, but it'll be graceful)

2180
01:26:33,872 --> 01:26:38,242
(The graduation of Palm Oil Prince who's been on the show for 6 years)

2181
01:26:39,512 --> 01:26:42,082
(A Beautiful Goodbye)

2182
01:26:42,552 --> 01:26:43,552
(Boom)

2183
01:26:43,553 --> 01:26:44,881
(Keeping the beat energetically)

2184
01:26:44,882 --> 01:26:46,892
(It's Dowoon?)

2185
01:26:47,522 --> 01:26:48,522
(It's been a while.)

2186
01:26:48,523 --> 01:26:49,792
(I'm Drummer Yoon Dowoon of DAY6.)

2187
01:26:51,192 --> 01:26:53,191
(He left early in the morning for the sea to fish.)

2188
01:26:53,192 --> 01:26:54,862
(An undisputed fishing genius)

2189
01:26:55,762 --> 01:26:58,532
(Today, he's humming at home.)

2190
01:26:59,602 --> 01:27:01,072
(Shall I show off my skills?)

2191
01:27:01,232 --> 01:27:02,902
(I haven't cooked in a while.)

2192
01:27:03,202 --> 01:27:05,042
(Skillful)

2193
01:27:05,602 --> 01:27:07,342
(I guess I'm a genius cook too.)

2194
01:27:10,882 --> 01:27:11,882
(What is this?)

2195
01:27:11,982 --> 01:27:13,312
(It's not what I had in mind.)

2196
01:27:14,382 --> 01:27:16,252
(Gosh, it's hot!)

2197
01:27:17,252 --> 01:27:18,522
(Clumsy)

2198
01:27:19,652 --> 01:27:21,091
(I guess I'm not a genius cook.)

2199
01:27:21,092 --> 01:27:22,152
(Sniffing)

2200
01:27:23,022 --> 01:27:25,161
(The place he has arrived to soothe his distressed heart)

2201
01:27:25,162 --> 01:27:26,792
(A music club)

2202
01:27:27,562 --> 01:27:29,092
(Enter the world of jazz.)

2203
01:27:30,102 --> 01:27:31,361
(The mood is free...)

2204
01:27:31,362 --> 01:27:32,501
(and sensual.)

2205
01:27:32,502 --> 01:27:33,602
That's cool too.

2206
01:27:33,672 --> 01:27:35,572
(Having a good time at a place he likes)

2207
01:27:36,772 --> 01:27:39,202
(It's twice as fun as he's with his friends.)

2208
01:27:40,072 --> 01:27:41,772
(Right then, a jam session starts.)

2209
01:27:42,572 --> 01:27:44,342
(Improvising and performing music spontaneously)

2210
01:27:44,612 --> 01:27:46,512
(Nervous)

2211
01:27:47,052 --> 01:27:48,682
(Shall we give it a try?)

2212
01:27:49,612 --> 01:27:52,789
(Fly to the Dowoon)
